window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b063-548434a5118db4d5.json"]={sha256:"548434a5118db4d5cf89ff11b87c72e634e06983fd3a86a328dd365a0abdd425",value:{"id":"b063","title":"巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統","titleEn":"Mega-column and outrigger structural systems","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以台北 101、哈里發塔與上海中心為例，從外伸臂約束核心轉角的旋轉彈簧模型與單道外伸臂的最佳高度出發，處理巨柱有效長度與樓板支撐力、外伸桁架穿入核心牆的力傳遞，再到差異縮短與延遲鎖定、雙層高桁架的焊接收縮、應變監測回推勁度、阻尼外伸臂，最後是外伸臂樓層的改裝管控與長期徐變監測。","summaryEn":"Using Taipei 101, Burj Khalifa and Shanghai Tower as examples, start from the rotational-spring model of how outriggers restrain core rotation and from the optimum level of a single outrigger, handle mega-column effective length and floor bracing forces and force transfer where outrigger trusses enter core walls, then differential shortening and delayed lock-off, weld shrinkage in two-storey trusses, strain monitoring to back-calculate stiffness and damped outriggers, ending with alteration control on outrigger floors and long-term creep monitoring.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-tall-systems","subcategoryTitle":"高層結構系統與減振","subcategoryTitleEn":"Tall-building structural systems and damping","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-tall-systems","learningTags":["structures","st-tall-systems","outrigger"],"architectureFamily":"outrigger","architectureNodes":[["核心筒","Core"],["外伸桁架","Outrigger trusses"],["巨柱","Mega-columns"],["帶狀桁架與樓板支撐","Belt trusses and floor bracing"],["延遲鎖定或阻尼接頭","Delayed lock-off or damper joints"],["基礎","Foundation"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,4],[4,2],[3,2],[2,5],[0,5]],"diagram":{"type":"outrigger","labels":["核心筒","外伸桁架","巨柱","帶狀桁架與樓板支撐","延遲鎖定或阻尼接頭"],"labelsEn":["Core","Outrigger trusses","Mega-columns","Belt trusses and floor bracing","Delayed lock-off or damper joints"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"單道外伸臂設計練習：某 300 m 高樓的核心筒 EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m²，均布風載 w = 150 kN/m，只有核心時頂部位移 Δ₀ = wH⁴/(8EI) = 150,000×300⁴/(8×7.0×10¹³) ≈ 2.17 m。兩側巨柱群各 EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N、間距 d = 40 m。外伸臂放在離地 a = 165 m 時，以 M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) 求得回復彎矩約 2.29 GN·m，每側巨柱群軸力約 2.29×10⁹/40 ≈ 57 MN，頂部位移減少約 54%，剩約 1.00 m。若改放頂部，只減少約 41%（剩約 1.28 m）；若巨柱軸向勁度減半，最佳位置仍在約 0.54H，但減少量降為約 39%（剩約 1.32 m）。這說明外伸臂的高度與巨柱勁度同樣重要，而且在這個簡化模型中最佳高度與柱勁度無關。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的設計。","textEn":"Single-outrigger exercise: a 300 m tower has a core with EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m² and a uniform wind load w = 150 kN/m, so the core alone drifts Δ₀ = wH⁴/(8EI) = 150,000×300⁴/(8×7.0×10¹³) ≈ 2.17 m at the top. The mega-column groups on each side have EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N and are d = 40 m apart. With the outrigger at a = 165 m, M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) gives a restoring moment of about 2.29 GN·m and a column-group force of about 2.29×10⁹/40 ≈ 57 MN, cutting top drift by about 54% to about 1.00 m. Placed at the top it cuts only about 41%, leaving about 1.28 m; with column axial stiffness halved the optimum stays near 0.54H but the reduction falls to about 39%, leaving about 1.32 m. Outrigger level and column stiffness therefore matter equally, and in this simplified model the optimum level does not depend on column stiffness. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design of any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b063-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角」與「單道外伸臂的最佳高度」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"How outriggers restrain core rotation\" and \"Optimum height of a single outrigger\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b063-v13-01","title":"外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"How outriggers restrain core rotation: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Core rotation and column axial stiffness” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"只有核心筒的高樓像一根懸臂梁，側力下底部彎矩全由核心承擔，頂部變位大。外伸臂是從核心伸出、連到周邊巨柱的深桁架或牆：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂一端上翹、一端下壓，迫使兩側巨柱一拉一壓，柱的軸向勁度因此變成抵抗核心轉動的旋轉彈簧，產生反向彎矩。這個反向彎矩減少外伸臂以下核心的彎矩與整棟樓的頂部變位，效果取決於柱的軸向勁度、柱距與外伸臂本身的勁度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A tower with only a core behaves like a cantilever: under lateral load the core carries the entire base moment and the top drifts a lot. An outrigger is a deep truss or wall extending from the core to perimeter mega-columns; when the core bends and rotates, one end of the outrigger lifts and the other presses down, forcing the columns on the two sides into tension and compression, so their axial stiffness becomes a rotational spring resisting core rotation and producing a counter-moment. That counter-moment reduces core moment below the outrigger and the building's top drift, by an amount that depends on column axial stiffness, column spacing and the outrigger's own stiffness. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Core rotation and column axial stiffness” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：柱群提供的旋轉勁度 K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Rotational stiffness from the column groups K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L).","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Core rotation and column axial stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-01-k1","title":"外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角","titleEn":"How outriggers restrain core rotation","text":"只有核心筒的高樓像一根懸臂梁，側力下底部彎矩全由核心承擔，頂部變位大。外伸臂是從核心伸出、連到周邊巨柱的深桁架或牆：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂一端上翹、一端下壓，迫使兩側巨柱一拉一壓，柱的軸向勁度因此變成抵抗核心轉動的旋轉彈簧，產生反向彎矩。","textEn":"A tower with only a core behaves like a cantilever: under lateral load the core carries the entire base moment and the top drifts a lot. An outrigger is a deep truss or wall extending from the core to perimeter mega-columns; when the core bends and rotates, one end of the outrigger lifts and the other presses down, forcing the columns on the two sides into tension and compression, so their axial stiffness becomes a rotational spring resisting core rotation and producing a counter-moment.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"How outriggers restrain core rotation\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。","只有核心筒的高樓像一根懸臂梁，側力下底部彎矩全由核心承擔，頂部變位大。","外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。"],"optionsEn":["An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness.","A tower with only a core behaves like a cantilever: under lateral load the core carries the entire base moment and the top drifts a lot.","An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只有核心筒的高樓像一根懸臂梁，側力下底部彎矩全由核心承擔，頂部變位大。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A tower with only a core behaves like a cantilever: under lateral load the core carries the entire base moment and the top drifts a lot. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b063-v13-02","title":"外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角：定量估算","titleEn":"How outriggers restrain core rotation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Core rotation and column axial stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：柱群提供的旋轉勁度 K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)。每側柱群 E = 35 GPa、A = 4 m²、兩側距離 d = 50 m、柱長（外伸臂到基礎）L = 200 m：K_θ = 35×10⁹×4×50²/(2×200) = 8.75×10¹¹ N·m/rad；核心在外伸臂處轉角 0.002 rad 時，回復彎矩 M = 8.75×10¹¹×0.002 = 1.75 GN·m。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Rotational stiffness from the column groups K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L). With E = 35 GPa and A = 4 m² per side, d = 50 m between sides and a column length from outrigger to foundation of L = 200 m, K_θ = 35×10⁹×4×50²/(2×200) = 8.75×10¹¹ N·m/rad; a core rotation of 0.002 rad at the outrigger gives a restoring moment M = 8.75×10¹¹×0.002 = 1.75 GN·m. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在結構模型中分別建立「只有核心」與「核心加外伸臂」兩種情況，比較頂層變位、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力；再以旋轉彈簧手算核對外伸臂回復彎矩，兩者差異過大時，檢查模型中外伸臂與柱的連接是否正確模擬。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build core-only and core-plus-outrigger cases in the structural model and compare top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial forces; then check the outrigger's restoring moment against the rotational-spring hand calculation, and if they differ widely, check whether the outrigger-to-column connection is modelled correctly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"柱群提供的旋轉勁度 K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)。每側柱群 E = 35 GPa、A = 4 m²、兩側距離 d = 50 m、柱長（外伸臂到基礎）L = 200 m：K_θ = 35×10⁹×4×50²/(2×200) = 8.75×10¹¹ N·m/rad；核心在外伸臂處轉角 0.002 rad 時，回復彎矩 M = 8.75×10¹¹×0.002 = 1.75 GN·m。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Rotational stiffness from the column groups K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L). With E = 35 GPa and A = 4 m² per side, d = 50 m between sides and a column length from outrigger to foundation of L = 200 m, K_θ = 35×10⁹×4×50²/(2×200) = 8.75×10¹¹ N·m/rad; a core rotation of 0.002 rad at the outrigger gives a restoring moment M = 8.75×10¹¹×0.002 = 1.75 GN·m. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"How outriggers restrain core rotation\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。","鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","柱群提供的旋轉勁度 K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)。"],"optionsEn":["If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter.","Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","Rotational stiffness from the column groups K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"柱群提供的旋轉勁度 K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Rotational stiffness from the column groups K_θ = E·A·d²/(2L). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b063-v13-03","title":"外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"How outriggers restrain core rotation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Core rotation and column axial stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在結構模型中分別建立「只有核心」與「核心加外伸臂」兩種情況，比較頂層變位、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力；再以旋轉彈簧手算核對外伸臂回復彎矩，兩者差異過大時，檢查模型中外伸臂與柱的連接是否正確模擬。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build core-only and core-plus-outrigger cases in the structural model and compare top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial forces; then check the outrigger's restoring moment against the rotational-spring hand calculation, and if they differ widely, check whether the outrigger-to-column connection is modelled correctly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計文件要說明外伸臂系統的力學假設（剛性或彈性、接合鎖定時機、樓板是否參與），並在接合細部圖上標明哪些螺栓在施工期保持可滑動、何時鎖定，由結構設計者確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design documents should state the mechanical assumptions of the outrigger system (rigid or flexible, when joints are locked, whether slabs participate) and mark on connection details which bolts stay free to slip during construction and when they are locked, confirmed by the structural designer.","failure":"注意干擾：若模型把外伸臂與柱的連接當成完全剛接，而實際接合因螺栓滑動或焊接變形而較柔，外伸臂效果被高估，核心與基礎承受的彎矩超過設計；樓板若被當成外伸臂的一部分卻沒有足夠的面內強度，地震時會在核心邊緣開裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the model treats the outrigger-to-column joint as fully rigid while the real joint is softer through bolt slip or weld distortion, the outrigger's benefit is overestimated and the core and foundation see more moment than designed; floor slabs counted as part of the outrigger without enough in-plane strength crack at the core edge in an earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在結構模型中分別建立「只有核心」與「核心加外伸臂」兩種情況，比較頂層變位、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力；再以旋轉彈簧手算核對外伸臂回復彎矩，兩者差異過大時，檢查模型中外伸臂與柱的連接是否正確模擬。","textEn":"Build core-only and core-plus-outrigger cases in the structural model and compare top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial forces; then check the outrigger's restoring moment against the rotational-spring hand calculation, and if they differ widely, check whether the outrigger-to-column connection is modelled correctly.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計文件要說明外伸臂系統的力學假設（剛性或彈性、接合鎖定時機、樓板是否參與），並在接合細部圖上標明哪些螺栓在施工期保持可滑動、何時鎖定，由結構設計者確認。","textEn":"Design documents should state the mechanical assumptions of the outrigger system (rigid or flexible, when joints are locked, whether slabs participate) and mark on connection details which bolts stay free to slip during construction and when they are locked, confirmed by the structural designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"How outriggers restrain core rotation\"?","options":["在結構模型中分別建立「只有核心」與「核心加外伸臂」兩種情況，比較頂層變位、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。"],"optionsEn":["Build core-only and core-plus-outrigger cases in the structural model and compare top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial forces.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在結構模型中分別建立「只有核心」與「核心加外伸臂」兩種情況，比較頂層變位、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力；再以旋轉彈簧手算核對外伸臂回復彎矩，兩者差異過大時，檢查模型中外伸臂與柱的連接是否正確模擬。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build core-only and core-plus-outrigger cases in the structural model and compare top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial forces; then check the outrigger's restoring moment against the rotational-spring hand calculation, and if they differ widely, check whether the outrigger-to-column connection is modelled correctly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b063-v13-04","title":"外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角：失效診斷","titleEn":"How outriggers restrain core rotation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「核心轉角與柱軸向勁度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Core rotation and column axial stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若模型把外伸臂與柱的連接當成完全剛接，而實際接合因螺栓滑動或焊接變形而較柔，外伸臂效果被高估，核心與基礎承受的彎矩超過設計；樓板若被當成外伸臂的一部分卻沒有足夠的面內強度，地震時會在核心邊緣開裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the model treats the outrigger-to-column joint as fully rigid while the real joint is softer through bolt slip or weld distortion, the outrigger's benefit is overestimated and the core and foundation see more moment than designed; floor slabs counted as part of the outrigger without enough in-plane strength crack at the core edge in an earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這個反向彎矩減少外伸臂以下核心的彎矩與整棟樓的頂部變位，效果取決於柱的軸向勁度、柱距與外伸臂本身的勁度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That counter-moment reduces core moment below the outrigger and the building's top drift, by an amount that depends on column axial stiffness, column spacing and the outrigger's own stiffness.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若模型把外伸臂與柱的連接當成完全剛接，而實際接合因螺栓滑動或焊接變形而較柔，外伸臂效果被高估，核心與基礎承受的彎矩超過設計；樓板若被當成外伸臂的一部分卻沒有足夠的面內強度，地震時會在核心邊緣開裂。","textEn":"If the model treats the outrigger-to-column joint as fully rigid while the real joint is softer through bolt slip or weld distortion, the outrigger's benefit is overestimated and the core and foundation see more moment than designed; floor slabs counted as part of the outrigger without enough in-plane strength crack at the core edge in an earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸臂如何約束核心筒轉角」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"How outriggers restrain core rotation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若模型把外伸臂與柱的連接當成完全剛接，而實際接合因螺栓滑動或焊接變形而較柔，外伸臂效果被高估，核心與基礎承受的彎矩超過設計。","外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If the model treats the outrigger-to-column joint as fully rigid while the real joint is softer through bolt slip or weld distortion, the outrigger's benefit is overestimated and the core and foundation see more moment than designed.","An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若模型把外伸臂與柱的連接當成完全剛接，而實際接合因螺栓滑動或焊接變形而較柔，外伸臂效果被高估，核心與基礎承受的彎矩超過設計；樓板若被當成外伸臂的一部分卻沒有足夠的面內強度，地震時會在核心邊緣開裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the model treats the outrigger-to-column joint as fully rigid while the real joint is softer through bolt slip or weld distortion, the outrigger's benefit is overestimated and the core and foundation see more moment than designed; floor slabs counted as part of the outrigger without enough in-plane strength crack at the core edge in an earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b063-v13-05","title":"單道外伸臂的最佳高度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Optimum height of a single outrigger: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「最佳外伸臂高度」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Optimum outrigger level” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂放在頂部時，連接的柱子最長、軸向勁度最小，回復彎矩只對頂部附近有效；放得太低時，柱子短而勁，但該處核心轉角很小，外伸臂幾乎不受力。最佳位置介於兩者之間：在均勻核心、均勻風載、外伸臂本身剛性的簡化模型中，單道外伸臂的最佳位置約在離地 0.54H（距頂約 0.46H），而且與柱的軸向勁度大小無關；多道外伸臂時大致沿高度平均分布。實務上還要配合機電層位置與建築使用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「最佳外伸臂高度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Put at the top, an outrigger engages the longest, axially softest columns and its restoring moment acts only near the top; put too low, the columns are short and stiff but the core barely rotates there, so the outrigger hardly works. The optimum lies between: in a simplified model with a uniform core, uniform wind and a rigid outrigger arm, a single outrigger works best about 0.54H above the base, about 0.46H below the top, independent of column axial stiffness, and several outriggers are best spread roughly evenly up the height. In practice the levels also follow mechanical floors and building use. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Optimum outrigger level” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：頂部位移減少 Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI，M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²))，θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Top-drift reduction Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI with M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) and θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI).","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「最佳外伸臂高度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Optimum outrigger level”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-05-k1","title":"單道外伸臂的最佳高度","titleEn":"Optimum height of a single outrigger","text":"外伸臂放在頂部時，連接的柱子最長、軸向勁度最小，回復彎矩只對頂部附近有效；放得太低時，柱子短而勁，但該處核心轉角很小，外伸臂幾乎不受力。最佳位置介於兩者之間：在均勻核心、均勻風載、外伸臂本身剛性的簡化模型中，單道外伸臂的最佳位置約在離地 0.54H（距頂約 0.46H），而且與柱的軸向勁度大小無關；多道外伸臂時大致沿高度平均分布。","textEn":"Put at the top, an outrigger engages the longest, axially softest columns and its restoring moment acts only near the top; put too low, the columns are short and stiff but the core barely rotates there, so the outrigger hardly works. The optimum lies between: in a simplified model with a uniform core, uniform wind and a rigid outrigger arm, a single outrigger works best about 0.54H above the base, about 0.46H below the top, independent of column axial stiffness, and several outriggers are best spread roughly evenly up the height.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單道外伸臂的最佳高度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Optimum height of a single outrigger\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。","巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。","外伸臂放在頂部時，連接的柱子最長、軸向勁度最小，回復彎矩只對頂部附近有效；放得太低時，柱子短而勁，但該處核心轉角很小，外伸臂幾乎不受力。"],"optionsEn":["An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there.","Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.","Put at the top, an outrigger engages the longest, axially softest columns and its restoring moment acts only near the top."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外伸臂放在頂部時，連接的柱子最長、軸向勁度最小，回復彎矩只對頂部附近有效；放得太低時，柱子短而勁，但該處核心轉角很小，外伸臂幾乎不受力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Put at the top, an outrigger engages the longest, axially softest columns and its restoring moment acts only near the top; put too low, the columns are short and stiff but the core barely rotates there, so the outrigger hardly works. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b063-v13-06","title":"單道外伸臂的最佳高度：定量估算","titleEn":"Optimum height of a single outrigger: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「最佳外伸臂高度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Optimum outrigger level” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：頂部位移減少 Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI，M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²))，θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI)。H = 300 m、EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m²、w = 150 kN/m、每側柱群 EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N、d = 40 m：無外伸臂時頂部位移 wH⁴/(8EI) ≈ 2.17 m；外伸臂在 a = 165 m 時減少約 54%，放在頂部只減少約 41%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Top-drift reduction Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI with M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) and θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI). With H = 300 m, EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m², w = 150 kN/m, EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N per column group and d = 40 m, the top drift without an outrigger is wH⁴/(8EI) ≈ 2.17 m; an outrigger at a = 165 m cuts it by about 54%, whereas one at the top cuts only about 41%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在結構模型中把外伸臂逐層移動，繪出頂部位移、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力隨高度的變化曲線，確認選定樓層接近最佳區間；多道外伸臂時再比較不同組合，並把機電層、避難層與建築使用的限制一起納入比選表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Move the outrigger floor by floor in the structural model and plot top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial force against its level, confirming that the chosen floor lies near the optimum band; for several outriggers compare combinations, including the constraints of mechanical floors, refuge floors and building use in the comparison table.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"頂部位移減少 Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI，M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²))，θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI)。H = 300 m、EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m²、w = 150 kN/m、每側柱群 EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N、d = 40 m：無外伸臂時頂部位移 wH⁴/(8EI) ≈ 2.17 m；外伸臂在 a = 165 m 時減少約 54%，放在頂部只減少約 41%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Top-drift reduction Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI with M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) and θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI). With H = 300 m, EI = 7.0×10¹³ N·m², w = 150 kN/m, EA = 1.4×10¹¹ N per column group and d = 40 m, the top drift without an outrigger is wH⁴/(8EI) ≈ 2.17 m; an outrigger at a = 165 m cuts it by about 54%, whereas one at the top cuts only about 41%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單道外伸臂的最佳高度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Optimum height of a single outrigger\", which statement holds?","options":["頂部位移減少 Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI，M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²))，θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI)。","外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。","外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。"],"optionsEn":["Top-drift reduction Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI with M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) and θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI).","The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better.","If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled."],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂部位移減少 Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI，M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²))，θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Top-drift reduction Δ_red = M·a·(H − a/2)/EI with M = θ_w(a)/(a/EI + 2a/(EA·d²)) and θ_w(a) = w·a·(3H² − 3Ha + a²)/(6EI). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b063-v13-07","title":"單道外伸臂的最佳高度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Optimum height of a single outrigger: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「最佳外伸臂高度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Optimum outrigger level” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在結構模型中把外伸臂逐層移動，繪出頂部位移、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力隨高度的變化曲線，確認選定樓層接近最佳區間；多道外伸臂時再比較不同組合，並把機電層、避難層與建築使用的限制一起納入比選表。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Move the outrigger floor by floor in the structural model and plot top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial force against its level, confirming that the chosen floor lies near the optimum band; for several outriggers compare combinations, including the constraints of mechanical floors, refuge floors and building use in the comparison table. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：概念設計階段就以簡化模型做外伸臂位置的敏感度分析，並與建築、機電團隊共同決定加強層樓層；比選紀錄保留在設計基準書，日後若需變更加強層位置，可據以快速評估影響。","observationEn":"Site practice: Run a sensitivity study of outrigger level with a simplified model at the concept stage and decide the strengthened floors jointly with the architecture and services teams; keep the comparison in the design basis so any later change in level can be assessed quickly.","failure":"注意干擾：若只因機電層剛好在頂部就把唯一的外伸臂放在那裡，減少的頂部位移可能比最佳位置少四分之一以上，核心與基礎因此必須加大；把外伸臂放得太低，則幾乎沒有減振效果卻增加了大量鋼材。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Putting the only outrigger at the top just because the plant room is there can forgo a quarter or more of the drift reduction available at the optimum, forcing a larger core and foundation; placing it too low adds a great deal of steel for almost no benefit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在結構模型中把外伸臂逐層移動，繪出頂部位移、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力隨高度的變化曲線，確認選定樓層接近最佳區間；多道外伸臂時再比較不同組合，並把機電層、避難層與建築使用的限制一起納入比選表。","textEn":"Move the outrigger floor by floor in the structural model and plot top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial force against its level, confirming that the chosen floor lies near the optimum band; for several outriggers compare combinations, including the constraints of mechanical floors, refuge floors and building use in the comparison table.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"概念設計階段就以簡化模型做外伸臂位置的敏感度分析，並與建築、機電團隊共同決定加強層樓層；比選紀錄保留在設計基準書，日後若需變更加強層位置，可據以快速評估影響。","textEn":"Run a sensitivity study of outrigger level with a simplified model at the concept stage and decide the strengthened floors jointly with the architecture and services teams; keep the comparison in the design basis so any later change in level can be assessed quickly.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單道外伸臂的最佳高度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Optimum height of a single outrigger\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在結構模型中把外伸臂逐層移動，繪出頂部位移、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力隨高度的變化曲線，確認選定樓層接近最佳區間。","機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Move the outrigger floor by floor in the structural model and plot top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial force against its level, confirming that the chosen floor lies near the optimum band.","Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在結構模型中把外伸臂逐層移動，繪出頂部位移、核心底部彎矩與巨柱軸力隨高度的變化曲線，確認選定樓層接近最佳區間；多道外伸臂時再比較不同組合，並把機電層、避難層與建築使用的限制一起納入比選表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Move the outrigger floor by floor in the structural model and plot top drift, core base moment and mega-column axial force against its level, confirming that the chosen floor lies near the optimum band; for several outriggers compare combinations, including the constraints of mechanical floors, refuge floors and building use in the comparison table. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b063-v13-08","title":"單道外伸臂的最佳高度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Optimum height of a single outrigger: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「最佳外伸臂高度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Optimum outrigger level” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只因機電層剛好在頂部就把唯一的外伸臂放在那裡，減少的頂部位移可能比最佳位置少四分之一以上，核心與基礎因此必須加大；把外伸臂放得太低，則幾乎沒有減振效果卻增加了大量鋼材。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Putting the only outrigger at the top just because the plant room is there can forgo a quarter or more of the drift reduction available at the optimum, forcing a larger core and foundation; placing it too low adds a great deal of steel for almost no benefit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：實務上還要配合機電層位置與建築使用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In practice the levels also follow mechanical floors and building use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只因機電層剛好在頂部就把唯一的外伸臂放在那裡，減少的頂部位移可能比最佳位置少四分之一以上，核心與基礎因此必須加大；把外伸臂放得太低，則幾乎沒有減振效果卻增加了大量鋼材。","textEn":"Putting the only outrigger at the top just because the plant room is there can forgo a quarter or more of the drift reduction available at the optimum, forcing a larger core and foundation; placing it too low adds a great deal of steel for almost no benefit.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單道外伸臂的最佳高度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Optimum height of a single outrigger\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。","若只因機電層剛好在頂部就把唯一的外伸臂放在那裡，減少的頂部位移可能比最佳位置少四分之一以上，核心與基礎因此必須加大。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.","Putting the only outrigger at the top just because the plant room is there can forgo a quarter or more of the drift reduction available at the optimum, forcing a larger core and foundation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只因機電層剛好在頂部就把唯一的外伸臂放在那裡，減少的頂部位移可能比最佳位置少四分之一以上，核心與基礎因此必須加大；把外伸臂放得太低，則幾乎沒有減振效果卻增加了大量鋼材。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Putting the only outrigger at the top just because the plant room is there can forgo a quarter or more of the drift reduction available at the optimum, forcing a larger core and foundation; placing it too low adds a great deal of steel for almost no benefit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b063-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力」與「外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces\" and \"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b063-v13-09","title":"巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"巨柱斷面很大，在每層樓板都有側向支撐時幾乎不會挫屈；但超高層常有挑空大廳、空中大廳或雙層機電層，若巨柱在數層甚至數十公尺範圍內沒有樓板拉住，有效長度大增，二階效應會明顯放大彎矩。支撐巨柱的樓板或繫梁也必須設計成能承受柱子傾向側移所產生的支撐力，一般以柱軸力的一小部分估計。台北 101 與上海中心都以帶狀桁架或樓板把巨柱與其他構件連成整體。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mega-columns are so large that they hardly buckle when every floor braces them laterally; but supertall towers often have atria, sky lobbies or double-height mechanical floors, and if a mega-column runs several storeys or tens of metres without a slab holding it, its effective length grows and second-order effects markedly amplify moments. Slabs or ties that brace mega-columns must also be designed for the bracing force generated by the column's tendency to sway, usually estimated as a small fraction of its axial load. Taipei 101 and Shanghai Tower both use belt trusses or slabs to tie mega-columns into the rest of the structure. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：P_cr = π²·EI/L²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: P_cr = π²·EI/L².","failure":"常見誤解：「巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-09-k1","title":"巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力","titleEn":"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces","text":"巨柱斷面很大，在每層樓板都有側向支撐時幾乎不會挫屈；但超高層常有挑空大廳、空中大廳或雙層機電層，若巨柱在數層甚至數十公尺範圍內沒有樓板拉住，有效長度大增，二階效應會明顯放大彎矩。支撐巨柱的樓板或繫梁也必須設計成能承受柱子傾向側移所產生的支撐力，一般以柱軸力的一小部分估計。","textEn":"Mega-columns are so large that they hardly buckle when every floor braces them laterally; but supertall towers often have atria, sky lobbies or double-height mechanical floors, and if a mega-column runs several storeys or tens of metres without a slab holding it, its effective length grows and second-order effects markedly amplify moments. Slabs or ties that brace mega-columns must also be designed for the bracing force generated by the column's tendency to sway, usually estimated as a small fraction of its axial load.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces\" is correct?","options":["巨柱斷面很大，在每層樓板都有側向支撐時幾乎不會挫屈。","巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。","外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Mega-columns are so large that they hardly buckle when every floor braces them laterally.","Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.","If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"巨柱斷面很大，在每層樓板都有側向支撐時幾乎不會挫屈；但超高層常有挑空大廳、空中大廳或雙層機電層，若巨柱在數層甚至數十公尺範圍內沒有樓板拉住，有效長度大增，二階效應會明顯放大彎矩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mega-columns are so large that they hardly buckle when every floor braces them laterally; but supertall towers often have atria, sky lobbies or double-height mechanical floors, and if a mega-column runs several storeys or tens of metres without a slab holding it, its effective length grows and second-order effects markedly amplify moments. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b063-v13-10","title":"巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：P_cr = π²·EI/L²。斷面 3.0 m × 3.0 m、E_eff = 30 GPa，EI = 30×10⁹×3⁴/12 ≈ 2.0×10¹¹ N·m²：L = 4.5 m 時 P_cr ≈ 98,700 MN；若無支撐長度 L = 60 m，P_cr ≈ 555 MN，軸力 400 MN 時比值 0.72，彎矩放大 1/(1 − 0.72) ≈ 3.6 倍。每層支撐力若取軸力 1%，約 4 MN。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: P_cr = π²·EI/L². For a 3.0 m × 3.0 m section with E_eff = 30 GPa, EI = 30×10⁹×3⁴/12 ≈ 2.0×10¹¹ N·m²: at L = 4.5 m P_cr ≈ 98,700 MN, but over an unbraced L = 60 m P_cr ≈ 555 MN, so a 400 MN axial load gives a ratio of 0.72 and moment amplification of 1/(1 − 0.72) ≈ 3.6. Taking 1% of the axial load as the bracing force gives about 4 MN per floor. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐一列出每支巨柱的無支撐長度，對挑空與機電層段做二階分析或挫屈分析，確認放大係數；支撐巨柱的樓板與繫梁以支撐力檢核面內強度與連接，並確認施工期間樓板未完成前的臨時支撐。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List the unbraced length of every mega-column, run second-order or buckling analyses for atrium and mechanical segments to confirm amplification factors, check the in-plane strength and connections of bracing slabs and ties for the bracing force, and confirm temporary bracing before slabs are complete during construction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"P_cr = π²·EI/L²。斷面 3.0 m × 3.0 m、E_eff = 30 GPa，EI = 30×10⁹×3⁴/12 ≈ 2.0×10¹¹ N·m²：L = 4.5 m 時 P_cr ≈ 98,700 MN；若無支撐長度 L = 60 m，P_cr ≈ 555 MN，軸力 400 MN 時比值 0.72，彎矩放大 1/(1 − 0.72) ≈ 3.6 倍。每層支撐力若取軸力 1%，約 4 MN。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"P_cr = π²·EI/L². For a 3.0 m × 3.0 m section with E_eff = 30 GPa, EI = 30×10⁹×3⁴/12 ≈ 2.0×10¹¹ N·m²: at L = 4.5 m P_cr ≈ 98,700 MN, but over an unbraced L = 60 m P_cr ≈ 555 MN, so a 400 MN axial load gives a ratio of 0.72 and moment amplification of 1/(1 − 0.72) ≈ 3.6. Taking 1% of the axial load as the bracing force gives about 4 MN per floor. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","P_cr = π²·EI/L²。","阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。"],"optionsEn":["Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","P_cr = π²·EI/L².","It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works."],"answer":1,"explanation":"P_cr = π²·EI/L²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"P_cr = π²·EI/L². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b063-v13-11","title":"巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐一列出每支巨柱的無支撐長度，對挑空與機電層段做二階分析或挫屈分析，確認放大係數；支撐巨柱的樓板與繫梁以支撐力檢核面內強度與連接，並確認施工期間樓板未完成前的臨時支撐。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List the unbraced length of every mega-column, run second-order or buckling analyses for atrium and mechanical segments to confirm amplification factors, check the in-plane strength and connections of bracing slabs and ties for the bracing force, and confirm temporary bracing before slabs are complete during construction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在結構圖上標示每支巨柱的支撐樓層與無支撐長度，任何挑空或樓板開口變更都必須回到結構設計者；施工計畫規定巨柱領先樓板的最大層數與臨時支撐方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the bracing floors and unbraced lengths of every mega-column on the structural drawings, route any atrium or slab-opening change back to the structural designer, and set in the construction plan the maximum number of floors mega-columns may run ahead of slabs, with the temporary bracing method.","failure":"注意干擾：建築變更新增挑空時若未通知結構設計者，巨柱失去數層支撐，二階彎矩可能讓柱在大震或強風時失穩；施工期間巨柱領先樓板太多，未支撐長度遠超設計，風力或吊裝碰撞就可能造成過大變形。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An architectural change that adds an atrium without telling the structural designer removes several floors of bracing, and second-order moments can destabilise the column in a major earthquake or strong wind; during construction, mega-columns that run far ahead of the slabs have unbraced lengths well beyond design, so wind or lifting impacts can cause excessive deformation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐一列出每支巨柱的無支撐長度，對挑空與機電層段做二階分析或挫屈分析，確認放大係數；支撐巨柱的樓板與繫梁以支撐力檢核面內強度與連接，並確認施工期間樓板未完成前的臨時支撐。","textEn":"List the unbraced length of every mega-column, run second-order or buckling analyses for atrium and mechanical segments to confirm amplification factors, check the in-plane strength and connections of bracing slabs and ties for the bracing force, and confirm temporary bracing before slabs are complete during construction.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在結構圖上標示每支巨柱的支撐樓層與無支撐長度，任何挑空或樓板開口變更都必須回到結構設計者；施工計畫規定巨柱領先樓板的最大層數與臨時支撐方式。","textEn":"Mark the bracing floors and unbraced lengths of every mega-column on the structural drawings, route any atrium or slab-opening change back to the structural designer, and set in the construction plan the maximum number of floors mega-columns may run ahead of slabs, with the temporary bracing method.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。","逐一列出每支巨柱的無支撐長度，對挑空與機電層段做二階分析或挫屈分析，確認放大係數。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue.","List the unbraced length of every mega-column, run second-order or buckling analyses for atrium and mechanical segments to confirm amplification factors, check the in-plane strength and connections of bracing slabs and ties for the bracing force, and confirm temporary bracing before slabs are complete during construction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐一列出每支巨柱的無支撐長度，對挑空與機電層段做二階分析或挫屈分析，確認放大係數；支撐巨柱的樓板與繫梁以支撐力檢核面內強度與連接，並確認施工期間樓板未完成前的臨時支撐。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List the unbraced length of every mega-column, run second-order or buckling analyses for atrium and mechanical segments to confirm amplification factors, check the in-plane strength and connections of bracing slabs and ties for the bracing force, and confirm temporary bracing before slabs are complete during construction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b063-v13-12","title":"巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「巨柱長細比與樓板支撐」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mega-column slenderness and floor bracing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"建築變更新增挑空時若未通知結構設計者，巨柱失去數層支撐，二階彎矩可能讓柱在大震或強風時失穩；施工期間巨柱領先樓板太多，未支撐長度遠超設計，風力或吊裝碰撞就可能造成過大變形。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An architectural change that adds an atrium without telling the structural designer removes several floors of bracing, and second-order moments can destabilise the column in a major earthquake or strong wind; during construction, mega-columns that run far ahead of the slabs have unbraced lengths well beyond design, so wind or lifting impacts can cause excessive deformation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：台北 101 與上海中心都以帶狀桁架或樓板把巨柱與其他構件連成整體。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Taipei 101 and Shanghai Tower both use belt trusses or slabs to tie mega-columns into the rest of the structure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"建築變更新增挑空時若未通知結構設計者，巨柱失去數層支撐，二階彎矩可能讓柱在大震或強風時失穩；施工期間巨柱領先樓板太多，未支撐長度遠超設計，風力或吊裝碰撞就可能造成過大變形。","textEn":"An architectural change that adds an atrium without telling the structural designer removes several floors of bracing, and second-order moments can destabilise the column in a major earthquake or strong wind; during construction, mega-columns that run far ahead of the slabs have unbraced lengths well beyond design, so wind or lifting impacts can cause excessive deformation.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨柱的有效長度與樓板支撐力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective length of mega-columns and floor bracing forces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["建築變更新增挑空時若未通知結構設計者，巨柱失去數層支撐，二階彎矩可能讓柱在大震或強風時失穩。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。"],"optionsEn":["An architectural change that adds an atrium without telling the structural designer removes several floors of bracing, and second-order moments can destabilise the column in a major earthquake or strong wind.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建築變更新增挑空時若未通知結構設計者，巨柱失去數層支撐，二階彎矩可能讓柱在大震或強風時失穩；施工期間巨柱領先樓板太多，未支撐長度遠超設計，風力或吊裝碰撞就可能造成過大變形。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An architectural change that adds an atrium without telling the structural designer removes several floors of bracing, and second-order moments can destabilise the column in a major earthquake or strong wind; during construction, mega-columns that run far ahead of the slabs have unbraced lengths well beyond design, so wind or lifting impacts can cause excessive deformation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b063-v13-13","title":"外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿在核心牆處集中巨大的拉壓力，必須以埋入牆內的鋼骨、鋼板與剪力釘把力量擴散到混凝土牆中；鋼構與混凝土牆的介面是整個系統最複雜的接合。常見做法是讓弦桿穿過核心牆並與牆內鋼板或型鋼連續，或在牆內設置鋼板剪力牆區段；上海中心的核心牆在加強層內即以鋼板或型鋼補強。穿牆處同時有大量鋼筋、預埋件與澆置空間的衝突，需要三維協調。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Outrigger chords and diagonals concentrate huge tension and compression where they meet the core, so steel sections, plates and shear studs embedded in the wall must spread that force into the concrete; the steel-to-concrete interface is the most complex connection in the system. Common solutions run the chord through the core wall continuously with embedded plates or sections, or form steel-plate shear-wall zones within the wall; Shanghai Tower's core walls are stiffened with steel plates or sections in the strengthened storeys. Where chords pass through, rebar, embeds and concreting space all compete, demanding three-dimensional coordination. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：剪力釘數量 n = F/Q_n。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Number of studs n = F/Q_n.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-13-k1","title":"外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞","titleEn":"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls","text":"外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿在核心牆處集中巨大的拉壓力，必須以埋入牆內的鋼骨、鋼板與剪力釘把力量擴散到混凝土牆中；鋼構與混凝土牆的介面是整個系統最複雜的接合。常見做法是讓弦桿穿過核心牆並與牆內鋼板或型鋼連續，或在牆內設置鋼板剪力牆區段；上海中心的核心牆在加強層內即以鋼板或型鋼補強。","textEn":"Outrigger chords and diagonals concentrate huge tension and compression where they meet the core, so steel sections, plates and shear studs embedded in the wall must spread that force into the concrete; the steel-to-concrete interface is the most complex connection in the system. Common solutions run the chord through the core wall continuously with embedded plates or sections, or form steel-plate shear-wall zones within the wall; Shanghai Tower's core walls are stiffened with steel plates or sections in the strengthened storeys.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls\" is correct?","options":["外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。","外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿在核心牆處集中巨大的拉壓力，必須以埋入牆內的鋼骨、鋼板與剪力釘把力量擴散到混凝土牆中；鋼構與混凝土牆的介面是整個系統最複雜的接合。","外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。"],"optionsEn":["If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter.","Outrigger chords and diagonals concentrate huge tension and compression where they meet the core, so steel sections, plates and shear studs embedded in the wall must spread that force into the concrete.","The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外伸桁架的弦桿與斜桿在核心牆處集中巨大的拉壓力，必須以埋入牆內的鋼骨、鋼板與剪力釘把力量擴散到混凝土牆中；鋼構與混凝土牆的介面是整個系統最複雜的接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Outrigger chords and diagonals concentrate huge tension and compression where they meet the core, so steel sections, plates and shear studs embedded in the wall must spread that force into the concrete; the steel-to-concrete interface is the most complex connection in the system. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b063-v13-14","title":"外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞：定量估算","titleEn":"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：剪力釘數量 n = F/Q_n。直徑 22 mm 剪力釘 A_sa ≈ 380 mm²，Q_n = 0.5·A_sa·√(f'c·E_c) = 0.5×380×√(60×36,000) ≈ 279 kN，但上限 A_sa·F_u = 380×450 ≈ 171 kN，取 171 kN；弦桿力 40 MN 需 40,000/171 ≈ 234 支，計入強度折減 0.65 約需 360 支。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Number of studs n = F/Q_n. A 22 mm stud has A_sa ≈ 380 mm² and Q_n = 0.5·A_sa·√(f'c·E_c) = 0.5×380×√(60×36,000) ≈ 279 kN, capped by A_sa·F_u = 380×450 ≈ 171 kN, so 171 kN governs; a 40 MN chord force needs 40,000/171 ≈ 234 studs, or about 360 with a resistance factor of 0.65. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿力在牆內的擴散與混凝土局部壓應力，確認剪力釘間距符合規範最小值；施工前做三維碰撞檢查與足尺模型或試作段，驗證鋼筋綁紮、剪力釘焊接與混凝土澆置的可行性，剪力釘以彎曲試驗抽查。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the spread of chord force within the wall and local concrete bearing stresses with a local finite-element model and confirm stud spacing meets code minimums; before construction run three-dimensional clash checks and a full-scale mock-up or trial section to prove rebar fixing, stud welding and concreting are feasible, and spot-check studs by bend testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"剪力釘數量 n = F/Q_n。直徑 22 mm 剪力釘 A_sa ≈ 380 mm²，Q_n = 0.5·A_sa·√(f'c·E_c) = 0.5×380×√(60×36,000) ≈ 279 kN，但上限 A_sa·F_u = 380×450 ≈ 171 kN，取 171 kN；弦桿力 40 MN 需 40,000/171 ≈ 234 支，計入強度折減 0.65 約需 360 支。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Number of studs n = F/Q_n. A 22 mm stud has A_sa ≈ 380 mm² and Q_n = 0.5·A_sa·√(f'c·E_c) = 0.5×380×√(60×36,000) ≈ 279 kN, capped by A_sa·F_u = 380×450 ≈ 171 kN, so 171 kN governs; a 40 MN chord force needs 40,000/171 ≈ 234 studs, or about 360 with a resistance factor of 0.65. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。","機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。","剪力釘數量 n = F/Q_n。"],"optionsEn":["If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled.","Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.","Number of studs n = F/Q_n."],"answer":2,"explanation":"剪力釘數量 n = F/Q_n。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Number of studs n = F/Q_n. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b063-v13-15","title":"外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿力在牆內的擴散與混凝土局部壓應力，確認剪力釘間距符合規範最小值；施工前做三維碰撞檢查與足尺模型或試作段，驗證鋼筋綁紮、剪力釘焊接與混凝土澆置的可行性，剪力釘以彎曲試驗抽查。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the spread of chord force within the wall and local concrete bearing stresses with a local finite-element model and confirm stud spacing meets code minimums; before construction run three-dimensional clash checks and a full-scale mock-up or trial section to prove rebar fixing, stud welding and concreting are feasible, and spot-check studs by bend testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：加強層的鋼構、牆內鋼板、鋼筋與澆置孔要在同一個三維模型中定案，並以試作段確認施工可行；澆置前設停止點，由結構設計者確認剪力釘、埋件與鋼筋的位置與檢驗紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Finalise strengthened-storey steel, embedded plates, rebar and placement openings in one three-dimensional model and prove constructability with a trial section; set a hold point before concreting at which the structural designer confirms stud, embed and rebar positions and inspection records.","failure":"注意干擾：剪力釘過密或鋼筋太擠時，混凝土在鋼板背後形成空洞，弦桿力無法有效傳入牆內，接合在設計載重前就局部滑移或壓碎；弦桿端部若沒有足夠的錨定長度，大地震時可能從牆中拔出。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Overcrowded studs or congested rebar leave voids behind the plates, so chord force cannot pass effectively into the wall and the joint slips or crushes locally before design load; chord ends without enough anchorage length can pull out of the wall in a major earthquake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿力在牆內的擴散與混凝土局部壓應力，確認剪力釘間距符合規範最小值；施工前做三維碰撞檢查與足尺模型或試作段，驗證鋼筋綁紮、剪力釘焊接與混凝土澆置的可行性，剪力釘以彎曲試驗抽查。","textEn":"Check the spread of chord force within the wall and local concrete bearing stresses with a local finite-element model and confirm stud spacing meets code minimums; before construction run three-dimensional clash checks and a full-scale mock-up or trial section to prove rebar fixing, stud welding and concreting are feasible, and spot-check studs by bend testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"加強層的鋼構、牆內鋼板、鋼筋與澆置孔要在同一個三維模型中定案，並以試作段確認施工可行；澆置前設停止點，由結構設計者確認剪力釘、埋件與鋼筋的位置與檢驗紀錄。","textEn":"Finalise strengthened-storey steel, embedded plates, rebar and placement openings in one three-dimensional model and prove constructability with a trial section; set a hold point before concreting at which the structural designer confirms stud, embed and rebar positions and inspection records.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls\"?","options":["以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿力在牆內的擴散與混凝土局部壓應力，確認剪力釘間距符合規範最小值。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Check the spread of chord force within the wall and local concrete bearing stresses with a local finite-element model and confirm stud spacing meets code minimums.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以局部有限元素模型檢查弦桿力在牆內的擴散與混凝土局部壓應力，確認剪力釘間距符合規範最小值；施工前做三維碰撞檢查與足尺模型或試作段，驗證鋼筋綁紮、剪力釘焊接與混凝土澆置的可行性，剪力釘以彎曲試驗抽查。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the spread of chord force within the wall and local concrete bearing stresses with a local finite-element model and confirm stud spacing meets code minimums; before construction run three-dimensional clash checks and a full-scale mock-up or trial section to prove rebar fixing, stud welding and concreting are feasible, and spot-check studs by bend testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b063-v13-16","title":"外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外伸桁架穿入核心牆」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outrigger chords embedded in core walls” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"剪力釘過密或鋼筋太擠時，混凝土在鋼板背後形成空洞，弦桿力無法有效傳入牆內，接合在設計載重前就局部滑移或壓碎；弦桿端部若沒有足夠的錨定長度，大地震時可能從牆中拔出。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Overcrowded studs or congested rebar leave voids behind the plates, so chord force cannot pass effectively into the wall and the joint slips or crushes locally before design load; chord ends without enough anchorage length can pull out of the wall in a major earthquake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：穿牆處同時有大量鋼筋、預埋件與澆置空間的衝突，需要三維協調。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Where chords pass through, rebar, embeds and concreting space all compete, demanding three-dimensional coordination.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"剪力釘過密或鋼筋太擠時，混凝土在鋼板背後形成空洞，弦桿力無法有效傳入牆內，接合在設計載重前就局部滑移或壓碎；弦桿端部若沒有足夠的錨定長度，大地震時可能從牆中拔出。","textEn":"Overcrowded studs or congested rebar leave voids behind the plates, so chord force cannot pass effectively into the wall and the joint slips or crushes locally before design load; chord ends without enough anchorage length can pull out of the wall in a major earthquake.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸桁架與核心牆的力傳遞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Force transfer between outrigger trusses and core walls\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","剪力釘過密或鋼筋太擠時，混凝土在鋼板背後形成空洞，弦桿力無法有效傳入牆內，接合在設計載重前就局部滑移或壓碎。","外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Overcrowded studs or congested rebar leave voids behind the plates, so chord force cannot pass effectively into the wall and the joint slips or crushes locally before design load.","The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剪力釘過密或鋼筋太擠時，混凝土在鋼板背後形成空洞，弦桿力無法有效傳入牆內，接合在設計載重前就局部滑移或壓碎；弦桿端部若沒有足夠的錨定長度，大地震時可能從牆中拔出。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Overcrowded studs or congested rebar leave voids behind the plates, so chord force cannot pass effectively into the wall and the joint slips or crushes locally before design load; chord ends without enough anchorage length can pull out of the wall in a major earthquake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b063-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定」與「雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off\" and \"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b063-v13-17","title":"差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「延遲鎖定接合」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Delayed lock-off connection” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"巨柱與核心筒的應力水準、材料與施工時間不同，在重力、徐變與乾縮下的縮短量也不同；外伸臂若在施工初期就把兩者剛接，差異縮短會讓外伸臂像槓桿一樣被強迫變形，產生與風、地震無關的巨大附加力。常見做法是施工期間讓外伸臂的一端以長槽孔或可調整接頭保持可動，等主要的重力縮短發生後（例如封頂後）再鎖定，或使用可多次調整的千斤頂接頭。鎖定時機是設計與施工共同決定的關鍵參數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「延遲鎖定接合」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mega-columns and the core differ in stress level, material and timing, so they shorten by different amounts under gravity, creep and shrinkage; if an outrigger rigidly joins them early in construction, differential shortening forces it to deform like a lever, inducing large extra forces unrelated to wind or earthquakes. The usual answer keeps one end of the outrigger free during construction through long slotted holes or adjustable joints, locking it after most gravity shortening has occurred, for example after topping out, or uses jacked joints that can be adjusted several times. The lock-off time is a key parameter decided jointly by design and construction. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Delayed lock-off connection” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：彈性縮短 δ = σ·L/E。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Elastic shortening δ = σ·L/E.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「延遲鎖定接合」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Delayed lock-off connection”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-17-k1","title":"差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定","titleEn":"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off","text":"巨柱與核心筒的應力水準、材料與施工時間不同，在重力、徐變與乾縮下的縮短量也不同；外伸臂若在施工初期就把兩者剛接，差異縮短會讓外伸臂像槓桿一樣被強迫變形，產生與風、地震無關的巨大附加力。常見做法是施工期間讓外伸臂的一端以長槽孔或可調整接頭保持可動，等主要的重力縮短發生後（例如封頂後）再鎖定，或使用可多次調整的千斤頂接頭。","textEn":"Mega-columns and the core differ in stress level, material and timing, so they shorten by different amounts under gravity, creep and shrinkage; if an outrigger rigidly joins them early in construction, differential shortening forces it to deform like a lever, inducing large extra forces unrelated to wind or earthquakes. The usual answer keeps one end of the outrigger free during construction through long slotted holes or adjustable joints, locking it after most gravity shortening has occurred, for example after topping out, or uses jacked joints that can be adjusted several times.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。","鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","巨柱與核心筒的應力水準、材料與施工時間不同，在重力、徐變與乾縮下的縮短量也不同。"],"optionsEn":["The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better.","Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","Mega-columns and the core differ in stress level, material and timing, so they shorten by different amounts under gravity, creep and shrinkage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"巨柱與核心筒的應力水準、材料與施工時間不同，在重力、徐變與乾縮下的縮短量也不同；外伸臂若在施工初期就把兩者剛接，差異縮短會讓外伸臂像槓桿一樣被強迫變形，產生與風、地震無關的巨大附加力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mega-columns and the core differ in stress level, material and timing, so they shorten by different amounts under gravity, creep and shrinkage; if an outrigger rigidly joins them early in construction, differential shortening forces it to deform like a lever, inducing large extra forces unrelated to wind or earthquakes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b063-v13-18","title":"差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「延遲鎖定接合」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Delayed lock-off connection” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：彈性縮短 δ = σ·L/E。巨柱 25 MPa、核心 12 MPa、E = 38 GPa、高度 200 m：巨柱約 0.000658×200,000 ≈ 131.6 mm，核心約 63.2 mm，相差 68.4 mm；計入徐變係數 1.5 約 171 mm。若立即鎖定，柱群 EA/L = 38×10⁹×4/200 = 7.6×10⁸ N/m，僅彈性差異就產生 7.6×10⁸×0.0684 ≈ 52 MN 的附加力。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Elastic shortening δ = σ·L/E. With 25 MPa in the mega-columns, 12 MPa in the core, E = 38 GPa and 200 m height: columns about 0.000658×200,000 ≈ 131.6 mm, core about 63.2 mm, a difference of 68.4 mm, or about 171 mm with a creep coefficient of 1.5. Locked immediately, a column group with EA/L = 38×10⁹×4/200 = 7.6×10⁸ N/m picks up 7.6×10⁸×0.0684 ≈ 52 MN from the elastic difference alone. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工階段分析（含材料時間效應）預測巨柱與核心在各施工時點的縮短，在代表性柱與核心牆埋設應變計、在外伸臂接頭設位移計；鎖定前比對實測差異與預測，確認剩餘差異引起的附加力在設計範圍內，才下達鎖定指令。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Predict mega-column and core shortening at each construction stage with a time-dependent construction-sequence analysis, embed strain gauges in representative columns and core walls, and fit displacement gauges at outrigger joints; before lock-off compare measured and predicted differences, issuing the lock-off instruction only when the extra force from the remaining difference is within design.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"彈性縮短 δ = σ·L/E。巨柱 25 MPa、核心 12 MPa、E = 38 GPa、高度 200 m：巨柱約 0.000658×200,000 ≈ 131.6 mm，核心約 63.2 mm，相差 68.4 mm；計入徐變係數 1.5 約 171 mm。若立即鎖定，柱群 EA/L = 38×10⁹×4/200 = 7.6×10⁸ N/m，僅彈性差異就產生 7.6×10⁸×0.0684 ≈ 52 MN 的附加力。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Elastic shortening δ = σ·L/E. With 25 MPa in the mega-columns, 12 MPa in the core, E = 38 GPa and 200 m height: columns about 0.000658×200,000 ≈ 131.6 mm, core about 63.2 mm, a difference of 68.4 mm, or about 171 mm with a creep coefficient of 1.5. Locked immediately, a column group with EA/L = 38×10⁹×4/200 = 7.6×10⁸ N/m picks up 7.6×10⁸×0.0684 ≈ 52 MN from the elastic difference alone. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off\", which statement holds?","options":["彈性縮短 δ = σ·L/E。","阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。","外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。"],"optionsEn":["Elastic shortening δ = σ·L/E.","It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works.","Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue."],"answer":0,"explanation":"彈性縮短 δ = σ·L/E。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Elastic shortening δ = σ·L/E. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b063-v13-19","title":"差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「延遲鎖定接合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Delayed lock-off connection” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工階段分析（含材料時間效應）預測巨柱與核心在各施工時點的縮短，在代表性柱與核心牆埋設應變計、在外伸臂接頭設位移計；鎖定前比對實測差異與預測，確認剩餘差異引起的附加力在設計範圍內，才下達鎖定指令。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Predict mega-column and core shortening at each construction stage with a time-dependent construction-sequence analysis, embed strain gauges in representative columns and core walls, and fit displacement gauges at outrigger joints; before lock-off compare measured and predicted differences, issuing the lock-off instruction only when the extra force from the remaining difference is within design. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要訂出外伸臂的暫時狀態、鎖定條件（例如封頂後且實測差異小於設定值）與施工期強風應變措施；鎖定作業設停止點，由結構設計者依監測資料簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The construction plan defines the outriggers' temporary state, the lock-off conditions (for example after topping out and with measured difference below a set value) and construction-stage storm measures; lock-off is a hold point signed by the structural designer on the basis of monitoring data.","failure":"注意干擾：若外伸臂在施工早期被焊死，數十公釐的差異縮短可能讓斜桿或接合在完工前就接近降伏，或在核心牆內造成裂縫；若鎖定太晚，施工期間遭遇強風時外伸臂無法發揮作用，核心單獨承受風力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If outriggers are welded solid early in construction, tens of millimetres of differential shortening can drive diagonals or joints close to yield before completion or crack the core walls; lock off too late and the outriggers cannot work during a construction-stage storm, leaving the core to resist wind alone. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工階段分析（含材料時間效應）預測巨柱與核心在各施工時點的縮短，在代表性柱與核心牆埋設應變計、在外伸臂接頭設位移計；鎖定前比對實測差異與預測，確認剩餘差異引起的附加力在設計範圍內，才下達鎖定指令。","textEn":"Predict mega-column and core shortening at each construction stage with a time-dependent construction-sequence analysis, embed strain gauges in representative columns and core walls, and fit displacement gauges at outrigger joints; before lock-off compare measured and predicted differences, issuing the lock-off instruction only when the extra force from the remaining difference is within design.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要訂出外伸臂的暫時狀態、鎖定條件（例如封頂後且實測差異小於設定值）與施工期強風應變措施；鎖定作業設停止點，由結構設計者依監測資料簽認。","textEn":"The construction plan defines the outriggers' temporary state, the lock-off conditions (for example after topping out and with measured difference below a set value) and construction-stage storm measures; lock-off is a hold point signed by the structural designer on the basis of monitoring data.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以施工階段分析（含材料時間效應）預測巨柱與核心在各施工時點的縮短，在代表性柱與核心牆埋設應變計、在外伸臂接頭設位移計。","外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Predict mega-column and core shortening at each construction stage with a time-dependent construction-sequence analysis, embed strain gauges in representative columns and core walls, and fit displacement gauges at outrigger joints.","An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以施工階段分析（含材料時間效應）預測巨柱與核心在各施工時點的縮短，在代表性柱與核心牆埋設應變計、在外伸臂接頭設位移計；鎖定前比對實測差異與預測，確認剩餘差異引起的附加力在設計範圍內，才下達鎖定指令。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Predict mega-column and core shortening at each construction stage with a time-dependent construction-sequence analysis, embed strain gauges in representative columns and core walls, and fit displacement gauges at outrigger joints; before lock-off compare measured and predicted differences, issuing the lock-off instruction only when the extra force from the remaining difference is within design. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b063-v13-20","title":"差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「延遲鎖定接合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Delayed lock-off connection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若外伸臂在施工早期被焊死，數十公釐的差異縮短可能讓斜桿或接合在完工前就接近降伏，或在核心牆內造成裂縫；若鎖定太晚，施工期間遭遇強風時外伸臂無法發揮作用，核心單獨承受風力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If outriggers are welded solid early in construction, tens of millimetres of differential shortening can drive diagonals or joints close to yield before completion or crack the core walls; lock off too late and the outriggers cannot work during a construction-stage storm, leaving the core to resist wind alone. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鎖定時機是設計與施工共同決定的關鍵參數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The lock-off time is a key parameter decided jointly by design and construction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若外伸臂在施工早期被焊死，數十公釐的差異縮短可能讓斜桿或接合在完工前就接近降伏，或在核心牆內造成裂縫；若鎖定太晚，施工期間遭遇強風時外伸臂無法發揮作用，核心單獨承受風力。","textEn":"If outriggers are welded solid early in construction, tens of millimetres of differential shortening can drive diagonals or joints close to yield before completion or crack the core walls; lock off too late and the outriggers cannot work during a construction-stage storm, leaving the core to resist wind alone.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差異縮短與外伸臂的延遲鎖定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential shortening and delayed outrigger lock-off\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","若外伸臂在施工早期被焊死，數十公釐的差異縮短可能讓斜桿或接合在完工前就接近降伏，或在核心牆內造成裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","If outriggers are welded solid early in construction, tens of millimetres of differential shortening can drive diagonals or joints close to yield before completion or crack the core walls."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若外伸臂在施工早期被焊死，數十公釐的差異縮短可能讓斜桿或接合在完工前就接近降伏，或在核心牆內造成裂縫；若鎖定太晚，施工期間遭遇強風時外伸臂無法發揮作用，核心單獨承受風力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If outriggers are welded solid early in construction, tens of millimetres of differential shortening can drive diagonals or joints close to yield before completion or crack the core walls; lock off too late and the outriggers cannot work during a construction-stage storm, leaving the core to resist wind alone. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b063-v13-21","title":"雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Outrigger erection and welding sequence” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"兩層高的外伸桁架構件又大又重，常拆成可吊裝的分段，在高空以全滲透焊或高強度螺栓接合。大量厚板焊接會產生收縮，若焊接順序不當，收縮累積會讓桁架節點偏離設計位置、在構件中留下殘餘應力，甚至把核心埋件或巨柱拉偏。施工方以預留收縮量、對稱焊接、先組後焊與臨時支撐控制幾何，並同時考慮塔吊在該半徑的吊重能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Two-storey outrigger members are large and heavy, so they are usually split into liftable segments joined at height by full-penetration welds or high-strength bolts. Welding so much thick plate causes shrinkage; with a poor sequence it accumulates, pulling truss nodes off their design positions, leaving residual stresses and even dragging core embeds or mega-columns out of line. Contractors control geometry with shrinkage allowances, symmetric welding, assembly before welding and temporary supports, while respecting tower-crane capacity at the working radius. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Outrigger erection and welding sequence” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：焊接收縮累積：若每道全滲透焊接頭橫向收縮約 1.5 mm，一條弦桿上有 6 個接頭，總收縮約 6×1.5 = 9 mm；跨距 15 m 的弦桿兩端因此靠近 9 mm，製造時應預留同量延長，或以對稱焊接讓兩端各收縮約 4.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Accumulated weld shrinkage: if each full-penetration joint shrinks about 1.5 mm transversely and a chord has 6 joints, the total is about 6×1.5 = 9 mm, pulling the ends of a 15 m chord 9 mm closer; fabrication should add the same allowance, or symmetric welding can split it into about 4.5 mm at each end.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Outrigger erection and welding sequence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-21-k1","title":"雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序","titleEn":"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses","text":"兩層高的外伸桁架構件又大又重，常拆成可吊裝的分段，在高空以全滲透焊或高強度螺栓接合。大量厚板焊接會產生收縮，若焊接順序不當，收縮累積會讓桁架節點偏離設計位置、在構件中留下殘餘應力，甚至把核心埋件或巨柱拉偏。","textEn":"Two-storey outrigger members are large and heavy, so they are usually split into liftable segments joined at height by full-penetration welds or high-strength bolts. Welding so much thick plate causes shrinkage; with a poor sequence it accumulates, pulling truss nodes off their design positions, leaving residual stresses and even dragging core embeds or mega-columns out of line.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses\" is correct?","options":["兩層高的外伸桁架構件又大又重，常拆成可吊裝的分段，在高空以全滲透焊或高強度螺栓接合。","鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。"],"optionsEn":["Two-storey outrigger members are large and heavy, so they are usually split into liftable segments joined at height by full-penetration welds or high-strength bolts.","Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩層高的外伸桁架構件又大又重，常拆成可吊裝的分段，在高空以全滲透焊或高強度螺栓接合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Two-storey outrigger members are large and heavy, so they are usually split into liftable segments joined at height by full-penetration welds or high-strength bolts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b063-v13-22","title":"雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序：定量估算","titleEn":"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Outrigger erection and welding sequence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：焊接收縮累積：若每道全滲透焊接頭橫向收縮約 1.5 mm，一條弦桿上有 6 個接頭，總收縮約 6×1.5 = 9 mm；跨距 15 m 的弦桿兩端因此靠近 9 mm，製造時應預留同量延長，或以對稱焊接讓兩端各收縮約 4.5 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Accumulated weld shrinkage: if each full-penetration joint shrinks about 1.5 mm transversely and a chord has 6 joints, the total is about 6×1.5 = 9 mm, pulling the ends of a 15 m chord 9 mm closer; fabrication should add the same allowance, or symmetric welding can split it into about 4.5 mm at each end. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：焊接前後量測節點座標與構件長度，比對預留收縮量是否正確；厚板焊接記錄預熱、層間溫度與焊接順序，完成後以超音波檢測並量測殘餘變形，偏差超過容許值時暫停後續焊接，由設計者評估。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure node coordinates and member lengths before and after welding to check the shrinkage allowance, record preheat, interpass temperature and welding sequence for thick plates, and after completion test ultrasonically and measure residual distortion, suspending further welding for the designer's assessment when deviations exceed tolerance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"焊接收縮累積：若每道全滲透焊接頭橫向收縮約 1.5 mm，一條弦桿上有 6 個接頭，總收縮約 6×1.5 = 9 mm；跨距 15 m 的弦桿兩端因此靠近 9 mm，製造時應預留同量延長，或以對稱焊接讓兩端各收縮約 4.5 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Accumulated weld shrinkage: if each full-penetration joint shrinks about 1.5 mm transversely and a chord has 6 joints, the total is about 6×1.5 = 9 mm, pulling the ends of a 15 m chord 9 mm closer; fabrication should add the same allowance, or symmetric welding can split it into about 4.5 mm at each end. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses\", which statement holds?","options":["機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。","焊接收縮累積：若每道全滲透焊接頭橫向收縮約 1.5 mm，一條弦桿上有 6 個接頭，總收縮約 6×1.5 = 9 mm。","外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.","Accumulated weld shrinkage: if each full-penetration joint shrinks about 1.5 mm transversely and a chord has 6 joints, the total is about 6×1.5 = 9 mm, pulling the ends of a 15 m chord 9 mm closer.","An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"焊接收縮累積：若每道全滲透焊接頭橫向收縮約 1.5 mm，一條弦桿上有 6 個接頭，總收縮約 6×1.5 = 9 mm；跨距 15 m 的弦桿兩端因此靠近 9 mm，製造時應預留同量延長，或以對稱焊接讓兩端各收縮約 4.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Accumulated weld shrinkage: if each full-penetration joint shrinks about 1.5 mm transversely and a chord has 6 joints, the total is about 6×1.5 = 9 mm, pulling the ends of a 15 m chord 9 mm closer; fabrication should add the same allowance, or symmetric welding can split it into about 4.5 mm at each end. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b063-v13-23","title":"雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Outrigger erection and welding sequence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"焊接前後量測節點座標與構件長度，比對預留收縮量是否正確；厚板焊接記錄預熱、層間溫度與焊接順序，完成後以超音波檢測並量測殘餘變形，偏差超過容許值時暫停後續焊接，由設計者評估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure node coordinates and member lengths before and after welding to check the shrinkage allowance, record preheat, interpass temperature and welding sequence for thick plates, and after completion test ultrasonically and measure residual distortion, suspending further welding for the designer's assessment when deviations exceed tolerance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：焊接程序書要指定焊接順序、預留收縮量、預熱與層間溫度與量測時機；高空吊裝與焊接依審查過的吊裝計畫進行，每個階段設停止點，由鋼構工程師與結構設計者確認幾何後才可續作。","observationEn":"Site practice: The welding procedure specifies sequence, shrinkage allowance, preheat and interpass temperature and measurement times; lifting and welding at height follow an approved lifting plan, with a hold point at every stage where the steel engineer and structural designer confirm geometry before work continues.","failure":"注意干擾：若從單側依序焊接整條弦桿，收縮會把桁架拉向一側，使與巨柱接合的孔位錯開，只能擴孔或現場切割；焊接殘餘應力與外伸臂的施工期附加力疊加，可能在厚板接頭產生裂紋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Welding a whole chord in sequence from one side pulls the truss to that side and misaligns the bolt holes at the mega-column, forcing reaming or site cutting; weld residual stresses added to construction-stage outrigger forces can crack thick-plate joints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"焊接前後量測節點座標與構件長度，比對預留收縮量是否正確；厚板焊接記錄預熱、層間溫度與焊接順序，完成後以超音波檢測並量測殘餘變形，偏差超過容許值時暫停後續焊接，由設計者評估。","textEn":"Measure node coordinates and member lengths before and after welding to check the shrinkage allowance, record preheat, interpass temperature and welding sequence for thick plates, and after completion test ultrasonically and measure residual distortion, suspending further welding for the designer's assessment when deviations exceed tolerance.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"焊接程序書要指定焊接順序、預留收縮量、預熱與層間溫度與量測時機；高空吊裝與焊接依審查過的吊裝計畫進行，每個階段設停止點，由鋼構工程師與結構設計者確認幾何後才可續作。","textEn":"The welding procedure specifies sequence, shrinkage allowance, preheat and interpass temperature and measurement times; lifting and welding at height follow an approved lifting plan, with a hold point at every stage where the steel engineer and structural designer confirm geometry before work continues.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。","焊接前後量測節點座標與構件長度，比對預留收縮量是否正確。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.","Measure node coordinates and member lengths before and after welding to check the shrinkage allowance, record preheat, interpass temperature and welding sequence for thick plates, and after completion test ultrasonically and measure residual distortion, suspending further welding for the designer's assessment when deviations exceed tolerance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"焊接前後量測節點座標與構件長度，比對預留收縮量是否正確；厚板焊接記錄預熱、層間溫度與焊接順序，完成後以超音波檢測並量測殘餘變形，偏差超過容許值時暫停後續焊接，由設計者評估。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure node coordinates and member lengths before and after welding to check the shrinkage allowance, record preheat, interpass temperature and welding sequence for thick plates, and after completion test ultrasonically and measure residual distortion, suspending further welding for the designer's assessment when deviations exceed tolerance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b063-v13-24","title":"雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序：失效診斷","titleEn":"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外伸桁架吊裝與焊接順序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outrigger erection and welding sequence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若從單側依序焊接整條弦桿，收縮會把桁架拉向一側，使與巨柱接合的孔位錯開，只能擴孔或現場切割；焊接殘餘應力與外伸臂的施工期附加力疊加，可能在厚板接頭產生裂紋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Welding a whole chord in sequence from one side pulls the truss to that side and misaligns the bolt holes at the mega-column, forcing reaming or site cutting; weld residual stresses added to construction-stage outrigger forces can crack thick-plate joints. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：施工方以預留收縮量、對稱焊接、先組後焊與臨時支撐控制幾何，並同時考慮塔吊在該半徑的吊重能力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Contractors control geometry with shrinkage allowances, symmetric welding, assembly before welding and temporary supports, while respecting tower-crane capacity at the working radius.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若從單側依序焊接整條弦桿，收縮會把桁架拉向一側，使與巨柱接合的孔位錯開，只能擴孔或現場切割；焊接殘餘應力與外伸臂的施工期附加力疊加，可能在厚板接頭產生裂紋。","textEn":"Welding a whole chord in sequence from one side pulls the truss to that side and misaligns the bolt holes at the mega-column, forcing reaming or site cutting; weld residual stresses added to construction-stage outrigger forces can crack thick-plate joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雙層高外伸桁架的吊裝與焊接順序」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Erection and welding sequence of two-storey outrigger trusses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若從單側依序焊接整條弦桿，收縮會把桁架拉向一側，使與巨柱接合的孔位錯開，只能擴孔或現場切割；焊接殘餘應力與外伸臂的施工期附加力疊加，可能在厚板接頭產生裂紋。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。"],"optionsEn":["Welding a whole chord in sequence from one side pulls the truss to that side and misaligns the bolt holes at the mega-column, forcing reaming or site cutting.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若從單側依序焊接整條弦桿，收縮會把桁架拉向一側，使與巨柱接合的孔位錯開，只能擴孔或現場切割；焊接殘餘應力與外伸臂的施工期附加力疊加，可能在厚板接頭產生裂紋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Welding a whole chord in sequence from one side pulls the truss to that side and misaligns the bolt holes at the mega-column, forcing reaming or site cutting; weld residual stresses added to construction-stage outrigger forces can crack thick-plate joints. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b063-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度」與「在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness\" and \"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b063-v13-25","title":"量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「外伸臂構件應變監測」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Strain monitoring of outrigger members” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂系統的實際效果取決於許多不確定因素：混凝土開裂後的核心勁度、接合的實際剛度、樓板參與程度與差異縮短的殘留量。在外伸臂斜桿、弦桿與相連巨柱上安裝應變計並量測溫度，可以把風或重力作用下的構件力量化，再與模型預測比較，回推系統的實際勁度分配。這些資料也是日後評估改裝或事件後狀態的基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外伸臂構件應變監測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"An outrigger system's real effectiveness depends on many uncertainties: cracked core stiffness, actual joint rigidity, slab participation and residual differential shortening. Strain gauges with temperature sensing on outrigger diagonals, chords and connected mega-columns turn wind or gravity effects into member forces that can be compared with model predictions to back-calculate the real stiffness distribution. The data also become the baseline for later assessment of alterations or post-event condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Strain monitoring of outrigger members” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：構件軸力 N = E·A·ε。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Member axial force N = E·A·ε.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外伸臂構件應變監測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Strain monitoring of outrigger members”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-25-k1","title":"量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度","titleEn":"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness","text":"外伸臂系統的實際效果取決於許多不確定因素：混凝土開裂後的核心勁度、接合的實際剛度、樓板參與程度與差異縮短的殘留量。在外伸臂斜桿、弦桿與相連巨柱上安裝應變計並量測溫度，可以把風或重力作用下的構件力量化，再與模型預測比較，回推系統的實際勁度分配。","textEn":"An outrigger system's real effectiveness depends on many uncertainties: cracked core stiffness, actual joint rigidity, slab participation and residual differential shortening. Strain gauges with temperature sensing on outrigger diagonals, chords and connected mega-columns turn wind or gravity effects into member forces that can be compared with model predictions to back-calculate the real stiffness distribution.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。","外伸臂系統的實際效果取決於許多不確定因素：混凝土開裂後的核心勁度、接合的實際剛度、樓板參與程度與差異縮短的殘留量。","阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。"],"optionsEn":["If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled.","An outrigger system's real effectiveness depends on many uncertainties: cracked core stiffness, actual joint rigidity, slab participation and residual differential shortening.","It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外伸臂系統的實際效果取決於許多不確定因素：混凝土開裂後的核心勁度、接合的實際剛度、樓板參與程度與差異縮短的殘留量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"An outrigger system's real effectiveness depends on many uncertainties: cracked core stiffness, actual joint rigidity, slab participation and residual differential shortening. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b063-v13-26","title":"量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度：定量估算","titleEn":"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外伸臂構件應變監測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Strain monitoring of outrigger members” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：構件軸力 N = E·A·ε。斜桿 A = 0.12 m²、E = 200 GPa，量得風作用下應變 150 με，N = 200×10⁹×0.12×150×10⁻⁶ = 3.6 MN；若模型預測同一風況為 4.0 MN，實際約為預測的 90%，代表接合或核心勁度與假設略有差異。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Member axial force N = E·A·ε. For a diagonal with A = 0.12 m² and E = 200 GPa, a measured wind strain of 150 με gives N = 200×10⁹×0.12×150×10⁻⁶ = 3.6 MN; if the model predicted 4.0 MN for the same wind, the actual force is about 90% of the prediction, indicating joint or core stiffness somewhat different from the assumption. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在同一斷面四周對稱安裝應變計以分離軸力與彎矩，並以溫度補償扣除日照影響；監測資料與風速計同步，挑選風向穩定的時段回歸出單位風壓下的構件力，再與模型比較，偏差超過約兩成時檢討模型假設。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mount gauges symmetrically around each section to separate axial force from bending, compensate for temperature to remove solar effects, synchronise with anemometers, and regress member force per unit wind pressure over periods of steady wind direction for comparison with the model, reviewing model assumptions when the difference exceeds about 20%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"構件軸力 N = E·A·ε。斜桿 A = 0.12 m²、E = 200 GPa，量得風作用下應變 150 με，N = 200×10⁹×0.12×150×10⁻⁶ = 3.6 MN；若模型預測同一風況為 4.0 MN，實際約為預測的 90%，代表接合或核心勁度與假設略有差異。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Member axial force N = E·A·ε. For a diagonal with A = 0.12 m² and E = 200 GPa, a measured wind strain of 150 με gives N = 200×10⁹×0.12×150×10⁻⁶ = 3.6 MN; if the model predicted 4.0 MN for the same wind, the actual force is about 90% of the prediction, indicating joint or core stiffness somewhat different from the assumption. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。","外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。","構件軸力 N = E·A·ε。"],"optionsEn":["Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue.","An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there.","Member axial force N = E·A·ε."],"answer":2,"explanation":"構件軸力 N = E·A·ε。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Member axial force N = E·A·ε. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b063-v13-27","title":"量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外伸臂構件應變監測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Strain monitoring of outrigger members” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在同一斷面四周對稱安裝應變計以分離軸力與彎矩，並以溫度補償扣除日照影響；監測資料與風速計同步，挑選風向穩定的時段回歸出單位風壓下的構件力，再與模型比較，偏差超過約兩成時檢討模型假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mount gauges symmetrically around each section to separate axial force from bending, compensate for temperature to remove solar effects, synchronise with anemometers, and regress member force per unit wind pressure over periods of steady wind direction for comparison with the model, reviewing model assumptions when the difference exceeds about 20%. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測計畫在設計階段就決定感測器位置、初讀時機（鎖定前後各一次）與資料格式；交接時把原始資料、處理方法與基準值一起移交營運單位，作為日後評估的依據。","observationEn":"Site practice: Decide sensor locations, initial-reading times (once before and once after lock-off) and data format at the design stage, and hand raw data, processing methods and baseline values to the operator at handover as the basis for future assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：應變計只裝在構件單側時，彎曲應變會被誤當成軸力；未做溫度補償時，日照造成的應變變化可能比風造成的還大，得出錯誤的勁度結論。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Gauges on one face only mistake bending strain for axial force; without temperature compensation, solar strain changes can exceed wind-induced ones and lead to wrong stiffness conclusions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在同一斷面四周對稱安裝應變計以分離軸力與彎矩，並以溫度補償扣除日照影響；監測資料與風速計同步，挑選風向穩定的時段回歸出單位風壓下的構件力，再與模型比較，偏差超過約兩成時檢討模型假設。","textEn":"Mount gauges symmetrically around each section to separate axial force from bending, compensate for temperature to remove solar effects, synchronise with anemometers, and regress member force per unit wind pressure over periods of steady wind direction for comparison with the model, reviewing model assumptions when the difference exceeds about 20%.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測計畫在設計階段就決定感測器位置、初讀時機（鎖定前後各一次）與資料格式；交接時把原始資料、處理方法與基準值一起移交營運單位，作為日後評估的依據。","textEn":"Decide sensor locations, initial-reading times (once before and once after lock-off) and data format at the design stage, and hand raw data, processing methods and baseline values to the operator at handover as the basis for future assessments.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness\"?","options":["在同一斷面四周對稱安裝應變計以分離軸力與彎矩，並以溫度補償扣除日照影響。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Mount gauges symmetrically around each section to separate axial force from bending, compensate for temperature to remove solar effects, synchronise with anemometers, and regress member force per unit wind pressure over periods of steady wind direction for comparison with the model, reviewing model assumptions when the difference exceeds about 20%.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在同一斷面四周對稱安裝應變計以分離軸力與彎矩，並以溫度補償扣除日照影響；監測資料與風速計同步，挑選風向穩定的時段回歸出單位風壓下的構件力，再與模型比較，偏差超過約兩成時檢討模型假設。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mount gauges symmetrically around each section to separate axial force from bending, compensate for temperature to remove solar effects, synchronise with anemometers, and regress member force per unit wind pressure over periods of steady wind direction for comparison with the model, reviewing model assumptions when the difference exceeds about 20%. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b063-v13-28","title":"量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外伸臂構件應變監測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Strain monitoring of outrigger members” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"應變計只裝在構件單側時，彎曲應變會被誤當成軸力；未做溫度補償時，日照造成的應變變化可能比風造成的還大，得出錯誤的勁度結論。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Gauges on one face only mistake bending strain for axial force; without temperature compensation, solar strain changes can exceed wind-induced ones and lead to wrong stiffness conclusions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些資料也是日後評估改裝或事件後狀態的基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The data also become the baseline for later assessment of alterations or post-event condition.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"應變計只裝在構件單側時，彎曲應變會被誤當成軸力；未做溫度補償時，日照造成的應變變化可能比風造成的還大，得出錯誤的勁度結論。","textEn":"Gauges on one face only mistake bending strain for axial force; without temperature compensation, solar strain changes can exceed wind-induced ones and lead to wrong stiffness conclusions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測外伸臂受力並回推系統勁度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Measuring outrigger forces to back-calculate system stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","應變計只裝在構件單側時，彎曲應變會被誤當成軸力；未做溫度補償時，日照造成的應變變化可能比風造成的還大，得出錯誤的勁度結論。","阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Gauges on one face only mistake bending strain for axial force.","It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應變計只裝在構件單側時，彎曲應變會被誤當成軸力；未做溫度補償時，日照造成的應變變化可能比風造成的還大，得出錯誤的勁度結論。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Gauges on one face only mistake bending strain for axial force; without temperature compensation, solar strain changes can exceed wind-induced ones and lead to wrong stiffness conclusions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b063-v13-29","title":"在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「阻尼外伸臂」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Damped outrigger” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"阻尼外伸臂把外伸臂端部與巨柱之間原本的剛性接合換成垂直的黏滯阻尼器：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂端部與巨柱之間產生相對垂直位移，阻尼器在這個相對運動中耗能，為整棟樓提供附加阻尼，同時避免剛性外伸臂傳遞過大的力。阻尼效果取決於阻尼器兩端的相對位移：外伸臂或柱子太柔時，阻尼器兩端一起動，就耗不了多少能量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「阻尼外伸臂」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A damped outrigger replaces the rigid joint between the outrigger tip and the mega-column with vertical viscous dampers: as the core bends and rotates, relative vertical movement arises between outrigger tip and column, and the dampers dissipate energy in that motion, adding damping to the whole building while avoiding the very large forces a rigid outrigger would transmit. The benefit depends on the relative displacement across the dampers: if the outrigger or columns are too flexible, both ends of the damper move together and little energy is dissipated. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Damped outrigger” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：附加阻尼比 ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Added damping ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s).","failure":"常見誤解：「阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「阻尼外伸臂」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Damped outrigger”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-29-k1","title":"在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器","titleEn":"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column","text":"阻尼外伸臂把外伸臂端部與巨柱之間原本的剛性接合換成垂直的黏滯阻尼器：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂端部與巨柱之間產生相對垂直位移，阻尼器在這個相對運動中耗能，為整棟樓提供附加阻尼，同時避免剛性外伸臂傳遞過大的力。阻尼效果取決於阻尼器兩端的相對位移：外伸臂或柱子太柔時，阻尼器兩端一起動，就耗不了多少能量。","textEn":"A damped outrigger replaces the rigid joint between the outrigger tip and the mega-column with vertical viscous dampers: as the core bends and rotates, relative vertical movement arises between outrigger tip and column, and the dampers dissipate energy in that motion, adding damping to the whole building while avoiding the very large forces a rigid outrigger would transmit. The benefit depends on the relative displacement across the dampers: if the outrigger or columns are too flexible, both ends of the damper move together and little energy is dissipated.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column\" is correct?","options":["阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。","機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。","阻尼外伸臂把外伸臂端部與巨柱之間原本的剛性接合換成垂直的黏滯阻尼器：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂端部與巨柱之間產生相對垂直位移，阻尼器在這個相對運動中耗能，為整棟樓提供附加阻尼，同時避免剛性外伸臂傳遞過大的力。"],"optionsEn":["It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works.","Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.","A damped outrigger replaces the rigid joint between the outrigger tip and the mega-column with vertical viscous dampers: as the core bends and rotates, relative vertical movement arises between outrigger tip and column, and the dampers dissipate energy in that motion, adding damping to the whole building while avoiding the very large forces a rigid outrigger would transmit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻尼外伸臂把外伸臂端部與巨柱之間原本的剛性接合換成垂直的黏滯阻尼器：核心彎曲轉動時，外伸臂端部與巨柱之間產生相對垂直位移，阻尼器在這個相對運動中耗能，為整棟樓提供附加阻尼，同時避免剛性外伸臂傳遞過大的力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A damped outrigger replaces the rigid joint between the outrigger tip and the mega-column with vertical viscous dampers: as the core bends and rotates, relative vertical movement arises between outrigger tip and column, and the dampers dissipate energy in that motion, adding damping to the whole building while avoiding the very large forces a rigid outrigger would transmit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b063-v13-30","title":"在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器：定量估算","titleEn":"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「阻尼外伸臂」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Damped outrigger” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：附加阻尼比 ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s)。模態質量 50,000 t、f = 0.15 Hz（ω = 0.942 rad/s）、頂部振幅 0.3 m：E_s = ½·M·ω²·X² ≈ 2.0 MJ；阻尼器總係數 c = 50 MN·s/m、相對位移 u = 0.05 m 時 E_d = π·c·ω·u² ≈ 0.37 MJ，ζ_add ≈ 1.5%；若 u 只有 0.02 m，ζ_add 降為約 0.24%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Added damping ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s). With a modal mass of 50,000 t, f = 0.15 Hz (ω = 0.942 rad/s) and a top amplitude of 0.3 m, E_s = ½·M·ω²·X² ≈ 2.0 MJ; with total damper coefficient c = 50 MN·s/m and relative displacement u = 0.05 m, E_d = π·c·ω·u² ≈ 0.37 MJ and ζ_add ≈ 1.5%; if u is only 0.02 m, ζ_add drops to about 0.24%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以包含阻尼器非線性特性的時間歷程分析計算阻尼器相對位移、力量與附加阻尼，確認在風與地震下都在阻尼器行程與力量範圍內；阻尼器做原型與逐件試驗，完工後以環境振動或強風紀錄辨識實際阻尼比，並與設計值比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute damper relative displacement, force and added damping with time-history analyses that include the dampers' nonlinear behaviour, confirming stroke and force limits are respected in wind and earthquake; test prototypes and every production damper, and after completion identify actual damping from ambient or strong-wind records for comparison with the design value.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"附加阻尼比 ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s)。模態質量 50,000 t、f = 0.15 Hz（ω = 0.942 rad/s）、頂部振幅 0.3 m：E_s = ½·M·ω²·X² ≈ 2.0 MJ；阻尼器總係數 c = 50 MN·s/m、相對位移 u = 0.05 m 時 E_d = π·c·ω·u² ≈ 0.37 MJ，ζ_add ≈ 1.5%；若 u 只有 0.02 m，ζ_add 降為約 0.24%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Added damping ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s). With a modal mass of 50,000 t, f = 0.15 Hz (ω = 0.942 rad/s) and a top amplitude of 0.3 m, E_s = ½·M·ω²·X² ≈ 2.0 MJ; with total damper coefficient c = 50 MN·s/m and relative displacement u = 0.05 m, E_d = π·c·ω·u² ≈ 0.37 MJ and ζ_add ≈ 1.5%; if u is only 0.02 m, ζ_add drops to about 0.24%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column\", which statement holds?","options":["附加阻尼比 ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s)。","外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。","巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。"],"optionsEn":["Added damping ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s).","An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness.","Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"附加阻尼比 ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Added damping ζ_add = E_d/(4π·E_s). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b063-v13-31","title":"在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「阻尼外伸臂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Damped outrigger” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以包含阻尼器非線性特性的時間歷程分析計算阻尼器相對位移、力量與附加阻尼，確認在風與地震下都在阻尼器行程與力量範圍內；阻尼器做原型與逐件試驗，完工後以環境振動或強風紀錄辨識實際阻尼比，並與設計值比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute damper relative displacement, force and added damping with time-history analyses that include the dampers' nonlinear behaviour, confirming stroke and force limits are respected in wind and earthquake; test prototypes and every production damper, and after completion identify actual damping from ambient or strong-wind records for comparison with the design value. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：阻尼外伸臂的設計基準要同時寫明附加阻尼目標、阻尼器相對位移範圍與行程限制；阻尼器的檢查、更換通道與鎖定程序在設計階段就預留，並納入維護手冊。","observationEn":"Site practice: The design basis of a damped outrigger should state the added-damping target, the range of damper relative displacement and stroke limits together; provide access, replacement routes and locking procedures for the dampers at the design stage and include them in the maintenance manual.","failure":"注意干擾：若外伸臂本身太柔，阻尼器兩端相對位移很小，附加阻尼遠低於預期；阻尼器在大地震時若超出行程而撞到止擋，力量突然增大，可能損壞外伸臂或巨柱接合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the outrigger itself is too flexible, the dampers see little relative displacement and added damping falls far short of expectations; dampers exceeding their stroke in a major earthquake hit their stops, abruptly raising force and possibly damaging the outrigger or column connection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以包含阻尼器非線性特性的時間歷程分析計算阻尼器相對位移、力量與附加阻尼，確認在風與地震下都在阻尼器行程與力量範圍內；阻尼器做原型與逐件試驗，完工後以環境振動或強風紀錄辨識實際阻尼比，並與設計值比較。","textEn":"Compute damper relative displacement, force and added damping with time-history analyses that include the dampers' nonlinear behaviour, confirming stroke and force limits are respected in wind and earthquake; test prototypes and every production damper, and after completion identify actual damping from ambient or strong-wind records for comparison with the design value.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"阻尼外伸臂的設計基準要同時寫明附加阻尼目標、阻尼器相對位移範圍與行程限制；阻尼器的檢查、更換通道與鎖定程序在設計階段就預留，並納入維護手冊。","textEn":"The design basis of a damped outrigger should state the added-damping target, the range of damper relative displacement and stroke limits together; provide access, replacement routes and locking procedures for the dampers at the design stage and include them in the maintenance manual.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以包含阻尼器非線性特性的時間歷程分析計算阻尼器相對位移、力量與附加阻尼，確認在風與地震下都在阻尼器行程與力量範圍內。","外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Compute damper relative displacement, force and added damping with time-history analyses that include the dampers' nonlinear behaviour, confirming stroke and force limits are respected in wind and earthquake.","The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以包含阻尼器非線性特性的時間歷程分析計算阻尼器相對位移、力量與附加阻尼，確認在風與地震下都在阻尼器行程與力量範圍內；阻尼器做原型與逐件試驗，完工後以環境振動或強風紀錄辨識實際阻尼比，並與設計值比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute damper relative displacement, force and added damping with time-history analyses that include the dampers' nonlinear behaviour, confirming stroke and force limits are respected in wind and earthquake; test prototypes and every production damper, and after completion identify actual damping from ambient or strong-wind records for comparison with the design value. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b063-v13-32","title":"在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器：失效診斷","titleEn":"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「阻尼外伸臂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Damped outrigger” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若外伸臂本身太柔，阻尼器兩端相對位移很小，附加阻尼遠低於預期；阻尼器在大地震時若超出行程而撞到止擋，力量突然增大，可能損壞外伸臂或巨柱接合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the outrigger itself is too flexible, the dampers see little relative displacement and added damping falls far short of expectations; dampers exceeding their stroke in a major earthquake hit their stops, abruptly raising force and possibly damaging the outrigger or column connection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：阻尼效果取決於阻尼器兩端的相對位移：外伸臂或柱子太柔時，阻尼器兩端一起動，就耗不了多少能量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The benefit depends on the relative displacement across the dampers: if the outrigger or columns are too flexible, both ends of the damper move together and little energy is dissipated.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「阻尼器裝在哪裡都一樣，只要阻尼係數夠大就有效。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"It makes no difference where dampers go; a large enough coefficient always works.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若外伸臂本身太柔，阻尼器兩端相對位移很小，附加阻尼遠低於預期；阻尼器在大地震時若超出行程而撞到止擋，力量突然增大，可能損壞外伸臂或巨柱接合。","textEn":"If the outrigger itself is too flexible, the dampers see little relative displacement and added damping falls far short of expectations; dampers exceeding their stroke in a major earthquake hit their stops, abruptly raising force and possibly damaging the outrigger or column connection.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「在外伸臂與巨柱之間加入阻尼器」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Placing dampers between outrigger and mega-column\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。","若外伸臂本身太柔，阻尼器兩端相對位移很小，附加阻尼遠低於預期；阻尼器在大地震時若超出行程而撞到止擋，力量突然增大，可能損壞外伸臂或巨柱接合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.","If the outrigger itself is too flexible, the dampers see little relative displacement and added damping falls far short of expectations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若外伸臂本身太柔，阻尼器兩端相對位移很小，附加阻尼遠低於預期；阻尼器在大地震時若超出行程而撞到止擋，力量突然增大，可能損壞外伸臂或巨柱接合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the outrigger itself is too flexible, the dampers see little relative displacement and added damping falls far short of expectations; dampers exceeding their stroke in a major earthquake hit their stops, abruptly raising force and possibly damaging the outrigger or column connection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b063-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控」與「外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors\" and \"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b063-v13-33","title":"外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alteration control on outrigger floors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂多設在機電層或避難層，這些樓層在營運期間經常需要更換設備、增設管線或改變用途。外伸桁架的斜桿與弦桿佔據大量空間，維修人員可能為了搬運設備或穿越管線而要求在構件上開孔、切割或焊接附掛物；任何一處削弱都可能切斷整個外伸臂的傳力路徑。因此外伸臂樓層在建築管理上必須被列為結構管制區，所有改裝都要經過結構審查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Outriggers usually sit in mechanical or refuge floors, which in service often need equipment replacement, new services or changes of use. Outrigger diagonals and chords occupy much of the space, and maintenance staff may ask to cut openings, trim members or weld attachments to move equipment or run services; any one weakening can sever the load path of the whole outrigger. Outrigger floors must therefore be designated structural control zones in building management, with every alteration subject to structural review. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Alteration control on outrigger floors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：開孔造成的淨斷面損失：弦桿斷面積 0.12 m²，若在 60 mm 厚的腹板開 600 mm 高的孔，損失 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m²，淨斷面剩 0.084 m²，約為原來的 70%；若原使用率為 0.8，開孔後使用率升為 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14，已超過容量。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Net-section loss from an opening: a chord of 0.12 m² with a 600 mm high hole cut in its 60 mm web loses 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m², leaving 0.084 m², about 70% of the original; a utilisation of 0.8 before the cut becomes 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14 after it, beyond capacity.","failure":"常見誤解：「機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Alteration control on outrigger floors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-33-k1","title":"外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控","titleEn":"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors","text":"外伸臂多設在機電層或避難層，這些樓層在營運期間經常需要更換設備、增設管線或改變用途。外伸桁架的斜桿與弦桿佔據大量空間，維修人員可能為了搬運設備或穿越管線而要求在構件上開孔、切割或焊接附掛物；任何一處削弱都可能切斷整個外伸臂的傳力路徑。","textEn":"Outriggers usually sit in mechanical or refuge floors, which in service often need equipment replacement, new services or changes of use. Outrigger diagonals and chords occupy much of the space, and maintenance staff may ask to cut openings, trim members or weld attachments to move equipment or run services; any one weakening can sever the load path of the whole outrigger.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂多設在機電層或避難層，這些樓層在營運期間經常需要更換設備、增設管線或改變用途。","機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。","外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。"],"optionsEn":["Outriggers usually sit in mechanical or refuge floors, which in service often need equipment replacement, new services or changes of use.","Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.","Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外伸臂多設在機電層或避難層，這些樓層在營運期間經常需要更換設備、增設管線或改變用途。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Outriggers usually sit in mechanical or refuge floors, which in service often need equipment replacement, new services or changes of use. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b063-v13-34","title":"外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控：定量估算","titleEn":"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alteration control on outrigger floors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：開孔造成的淨斷面損失：弦桿斷面積 0.12 m²，若在 60 mm 厚的腹板開 600 mm 高的孔，損失 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m²，淨斷面剩 0.084 m²，約為原來的 70%；若原使用率為 0.8，開孔後使用率升為 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14，已超過容量。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Net-section loss from an opening: a chord of 0.12 m² with a 600 mm high hole cut in its 60 mm web loses 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m², leaving 0.084 m², about 70% of the original; a utilisation of 0.8 before the cut becomes 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14 after it, beyond capacity. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在外伸臂樓層的構件上以顏色或標牌標示「結構關鍵構件，禁止切割與焊接」，定期巡檢是否有未經許可的開孔、附掛或腐蝕；改裝申請附結構計算，完成後由結構工程師現場驗收並更新竣工圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark outrigger-floor members with colour codes or signs reading critical structural member, no cutting or welding; inspect periodically for unauthorised openings, attachments or corrosion; require structural calculations with alteration requests and have the structural engineer accept the work on site and update the as-built drawings.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"開孔造成的淨斷面損失：弦桿斷面積 0.12 m²，若在 60 mm 厚的腹板開 600 mm 高的孔，損失 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m²，淨斷面剩 0.084 m²，約為原來的 70%；若原使用率為 0.8，開孔後使用率升為 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14，已超過容量。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Net-section loss from an opening: a chord of 0.12 m² with a 600 mm high hole cut in its 60 mm web loses 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m², leaving 0.084 m², about 70% of the original; a utilisation of 0.8 before the cut becomes 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14 after it, beyond capacity. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂放在建築頂部效果最好，因為那裡轉角最大。","開孔造成的淨斷面損失：弦桿斷面積 0.12 m²，若在 60 mm 厚的腹板開 600 mm 高的孔，損失 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m²，淨斷面剩 0.084 m²，約為原來的 70%。","外伸桁架只要鋼構夠強，接到混凝土核心的方式不重要。"],"optionsEn":["An outrigger works best at the top of the building because rotation is largest there.","Net-section loss from an opening: a chord of 0.12 m² with a 600 mm high hole cut in its 60 mm web loses 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m², leaving 0.084 m², about 70% of the original.","If the outrigger steel is strong enough, the way it connects to the concrete core does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開孔造成的淨斷面損失：弦桿斷面積 0.12 m²，若在 60 mm 厚的腹板開 600 mm 高的孔，損失 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m²，淨斷面剩 0.084 m²，約為原來的 70%；若原使用率為 0.8，開孔後使用率升為 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14，已超過容量。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Net-section loss from an opening: a chord of 0.12 m² with a 600 mm high hole cut in its 60 mm web loses 0.6×0.06 = 0.036 m², leaving 0.084 m², about 70% of the original; a utilisation of 0.8 before the cut becomes 0.8/0.7 ≈ 1.14 after it, beyond capacity. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b063-v13-35","title":"外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alteration control on outrigger floors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在外伸臂樓層的構件上以顏色或標牌標示「結構關鍵構件，禁止切割與焊接」，定期巡檢是否有未經許可的開孔、附掛或腐蝕；改裝申請附結構計算，完成後由結構工程師現場驗收並更新竣工圖。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark outrigger-floor members with colour codes or signs reading critical structural member, no cutting or welding; inspect periodically for unauthorised openings, attachments or corrosion; require structural calculations with alteration requests and have the structural engineer accept the work on site and update the as-built drawings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：營運手冊附外伸臂樓層的結構管制圖、可用的設備搬運路徑與預留孔位置，任何改裝都須取得結構工程師簽認；設備更換路線應在設計階段就預留，避免日後切割構件。","observationEn":"Site practice: The operations manual includes structural control plans for outrigger floors, the permitted equipment routes and the provided openings, with every alteration needing the structural engineer's sign-off; plan equipment replacement routes at the design stage so members never need cutting later.","failure":"注意干擾：機電承包商為了更換大型設備而切斷一根斜桿，外伸臂的力流被打斷，強風或地震時核心與基礎承受遠超設計的彎矩；這種損傷平時看不出來，只有在極端事件中才會暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A services contractor cutting through a diagonal to replace large equipment interrupts the outrigger's force flow, so in strong wind or earthquakes the core and foundation take moments far beyond design; the damage is invisible day to day and exposed only in an extreme event. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在外伸臂樓層的構件上以顏色或標牌標示「結構關鍵構件，禁止切割與焊接」，定期巡檢是否有未經許可的開孔、附掛或腐蝕；改裝申請附結構計算，完成後由結構工程師現場驗收並更新竣工圖。","textEn":"Mark outrigger-floor members with colour codes or signs reading critical structural member, no cutting or welding; inspect periodically for unauthorised openings, attachments or corrosion; require structural calculations with alteration requests and have the structural engineer accept the work on site and update the as-built drawings.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"營運手冊附外伸臂樓層的結構管制圖、可用的設備搬運路徑與預留孔位置，任何改裝都須取得結構工程師簽認；設備更換路線應在設計階段就預留，避免日後切割構件。","textEn":"The operations manual includes structural control plans for outrigger floors, the permitted equipment routes and the provided openings, with every alteration needing the structural engineer's sign-off; plan equipment replacement routes at the design stage so members never need cutting later.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","鋼構在工廠做得精準，現場焊接不會改變幾何。","在外伸臂樓層的構件上以顏色或標牌標示「結構關鍵構件，禁止切割與焊接」，定期巡檢是否有未經許可的開孔、附掛或腐蝕。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Steel fabricated accurately in the shop keeps its geometry through site welding.","Mark outrigger-floor members with colour codes or signs reading critical structural member, no cutting or welding."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在外伸臂樓層的構件上以顏色或標牌標示「結構關鍵構件，禁止切割與焊接」，定期巡檢是否有未經許可的開孔、附掛或腐蝕；改裝申請附結構計算，完成後由結構工程師現場驗收並更新竣工圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark outrigger-floor members with colour codes or signs reading critical structural member, no cutting or welding; inspect periodically for unauthorised openings, attachments or corrosion; require structural calculations with alteration requests and have the structural engineer accept the work on site and update the as-built drawings. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b063-v13-36","title":"外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控：失效診斷","titleEn":"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外伸臂樓層的改裝管控」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alteration control on outrigger floors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"機電承包商為了更換大型設備而切斷一根斜桿，外伸臂的力流被打斷，強風或地震時核心與基礎承受遠超設計的彎矩；這種損傷平時看不出來，只有在極端事件中才會暴露。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A services contractor cutting through a diagonal to replace large equipment interrupts the outrigger's force flow, so in strong wind or earthquakes the core and foundation take moments far beyond design; the damage is invisible day to day and exposed only in an extreme event. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此外伸臂樓層在建築管理上必須被列為結構管制區，所有改裝都要經過結構審查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Outrigger floors must therefore be designated structural control zones in building management, with every alteration subject to structural review.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「機電層是設備空間，構件開孔只是施工方便的小事。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Mechanical floors are equipment space, so cutting members is a minor matter of convenience.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"機電承包商為了更換大型設備而切斷一根斜桿，外伸臂的力流被打斷，強風或地震時核心與基礎承受遠超設計的彎矩；這種損傷平時看不出來，只有在極端事件中才會暴露。","textEn":"A services contractor cutting through a diagonal to replace large equipment interrupts the outrigger's force flow, so in strong wind or earthquakes the core and foundation take moments far beyond design; the damage is invisible day to day and exposed only in an extreme event.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸臂樓層的使用限制與改裝管控」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Use restrictions and alteration control on outrigger floors\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["機電承包商為了更換大型設備而切斷一根斜桿，外伸臂的力流被打斷，強風或地震時核心與基礎承受遠超設計的彎矩；這種損傷平時看不出來，只有在極端事件中才會暴露。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。"],"optionsEn":["A services contractor cutting through a diagonal to replace large equipment interrupts the outrigger's force flow, so in strong wind or earthquakes the core and foundation take moments far beyond design.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue."],"answer":0,"explanation":"機電承包商為了更換大型設備而切斷一根斜桿，外伸臂的力流被打斷，強風或地震時核心與基礎承受遠超設計的彎矩；這種損傷平時看不出來，只有在極端事件中才會暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A services contractor cutting through a diagonal to replace large equipment interrupts the outrigger's force flow, so in strong wind or earthquakes the core and foundation take moments far beyond design; the damage is invisible day to day and exposed only in an extreme event. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b063-v13-37","title":"外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「長期徐變監測」如何影響巨型柱—外伸臂結構系統的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-term creep monitoring” governs force, deformation or durability in “Mega-column and outrigger structural systems”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂鎖定之後，巨柱與核心的徐變與乾縮仍會持續數年至十數年，殘留的差異縮短會慢慢增加外伸臂與巨柱的附加力，也可能讓樓板邊緣傾斜。長期監測以應變計、精密水準與接頭位移計追蹤這個過程，並與時間相依分析比較；交接文件要讓營運單位知道哪些數值屬於正常發展、何時需要請結構顧問評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「長期徐變監測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After lock-off, creep and shrinkage of mega-columns and core continue for years or even more than a decade, and the residual differential shortening slowly adds force to outriggers and columns and can tilt slab edges. Long-term monitoring with strain gauges, precise levelling and joint displacement gauges tracks this process against time-dependent analysis, and handover documents must tell the operator which values are normal development and when to call in the structural consultant. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Long-term creep monitoring” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：ACI 209 徐變發展 φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶)，φ∞ = 2.35：t = 30 天時 φ ≈ 1.02，1 年時 ≈ 1.82，10 年時 ≈ 2.19。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: ACI 209 creep development φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶) with φ∞ = 2.35: φ ≈ 1.02 at 30 days, ≈ 1.82 at 1 year and ≈ 2.19 at 10 years.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「長期徐變監測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Long-term creep monitoring”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-37-k1","title":"外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接","titleEn":"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems","text":"外伸臂鎖定之後，巨柱與核心的徐變與乾縮仍會持續數年至十數年，殘留的差異縮短會慢慢增加外伸臂與巨柱的附加力，也可能讓樓板邊緣傾斜。長期監測以應變計、精密水準與接頭位移計追蹤這個過程，並與時間相依分析比較；交接文件要讓營運單位知道哪些數值屬於正常發展、何時需要請結構顧問評估。","textEn":"After lock-off, creep and shrinkage of mega-columns and core continue for years or even more than a decade, and the residual differential shortening slowly adds force to outriggers and columns and can tilt slab edges. Long-term monitoring with strain gauges, precise levelling and joint displacement gauges tracks this process against time-dependent analysis, and handover documents must tell the operator which values are normal development and when to call in the structural consultant.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。","外伸臂鎖定之後，巨柱與核心的徐變與乾縮仍會持續數年至十數年，殘留的差異縮短會慢慢增加外伸臂與巨柱的附加力，也可能讓樓板邊緣傾斜。","外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue.","After lock-off, creep and shrinkage of mega-columns and core continue for years or even more than a decade, and the residual differential shortening slowly adds force to outriggers and columns and can tilt slab edges.","An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外伸臂鎖定之後，巨柱與核心的徐變與乾縮仍會持續數年至十數年，殘留的差異縮短會慢慢增加外伸臂與巨柱的附加力，也可能讓樓板邊緣傾斜。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After lock-off, creep and shrinkage of mega-columns and core continue for years or even more than a decade, and the residual differential shortening slowly adds force to outriggers and columns and can tilt slab edges. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b063-v13-38","title":"外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長期徐變監測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-term creep monitoring” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：ACI 209 徐變發展 φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶)，φ∞ = 2.35：t = 30 天時 φ ≈ 1.02，1 年時 ≈ 1.82，10 年時 ≈ 2.19。若加載 1 年後才鎖定，剩下的徐變只佔 10 年值的 (2.19 − 1.82)/2.19 ≈ 17%，鎖定後的附加力也大致同比例減少。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: ACI 209 creep development φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶) with φ∞ = 2.35: φ ≈ 1.02 at 30 days, ≈ 1.82 at 1 year and ≈ 2.19 at 10 years. Locking off one year after loading leaves only (2.19 − 1.82)/2.19 ≈ 17% of the 10-year creep, and the force added after lock-off falls roughly in proportion. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每年以精密水準量測巨柱與核心在代表樓層的高程差，並讀取應變計與接頭位移計，與時間相依分析的預測曲線比較；發展速率異常（例如某支巨柱持續快於其他柱）時，檢查是否有局部超載或材料問題。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Each year measure level differences between mega-columns and core on representative floors by precise levelling and read strain gauges and joint displacement gauges, comparing with the predicted time-dependent curves; if a rate is abnormal, such as one column persistently outpacing the others, check for local overloading or material problems.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"ACI 209 徐變發展 φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶)，φ∞ = 2.35：t = 30 天時 φ ≈ 1.02，1 年時 ≈ 1.82，10 年時 ≈ 2.19。若加載 1 年後才鎖定，剩下的徐變只佔 10 年值的 (2.19 − 1.82)/2.19 ≈ 17%，鎖定後的附加力也大致同比例減少。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"ACI 209 creep development φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶) with φ∞ = 2.35: φ ≈ 1.02 at 30 days, ≈ 1.82 at 1 year and ≈ 2.19 at 10 years. Locking off one year after loading leaves only (2.19 − 1.82)/2.19 ≈ 17% of the 10-year creep, and the force added after lock-off falls roughly in proportion. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems\", which statement holds?","options":["巨柱斷面這麼大，不可能挫屈，所以樓板支撐無關緊要。","外伸臂越早鎖定越好，可以讓結構越早完整。","ACI 209 徐變發展 φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶)，φ∞ = 2.35：t = 30 天時 φ ≈ 1.02，1 年時 ≈ 1.82，10 年時 ≈ 2.19。"],"optionsEn":["Mega-columns are so large they cannot buckle, so floor bracing does not matter.","The earlier an outrigger is locked, the sooner the structure is complete, so earlier is better.","ACI 209 creep development φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶) with φ∞ = 2.35: φ ≈ 1.02 at 30 days, ≈ 1.82 at 1 year and ≈ 2.19 at 10 years."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ACI 209 徐變發展 φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶)，φ∞ = 2.35：t = 30 天時 φ ≈ 1.02，1 年時 ≈ 1.82，10 年時 ≈ 2.19。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"ACI 209 creep development φ(t) = φ∞·t⁰·⁶/(10 + t⁰·⁶) with φ∞ = 2.35: φ ≈ 1.02 at 30 days, ≈ 1.82 at 1 year and ≈ 2.19 at 10 years. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b063-v13-39","title":"外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長期徐變監測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-term creep monitoring” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每年以精密水準量測巨柱與核心在代表樓層的高程差，並讀取應變計與接頭位移計，與時間相依分析的預測曲線比較；發展速率異常（例如某支巨柱持續快於其他柱）時，檢查是否有局部超載或材料問題。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Each year measure level differences between mega-columns and core on representative floors by precise levelling and read strain gauges and joint displacement gauges, comparing with the predicted time-dependent curves; if a rate is abnormal, such as one column persistently outpacing the others, check for local overloading or material problems. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件包含鎖定時的實測差異、預測的長期曲線、監測點位置與允收範圍，以及超出範圍時的處理流程；監測至少持續到徐變發展趨緩，並由結構顧問定期審閱。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents include the measured difference at lock-off, the predicted long-term curves, monitoring locations and acceptance ranges, and the procedure when values fall outside them; continue monitoring at least until creep growth levels off, with periodic review by the structural consultant.","failure":"注意干擾：若沒有長期監測，殘留差異縮短造成的樓板傾斜與帷幕接縫變形會被誤認為施工瑕疵而反覆修補；外伸臂附加力超出預期，也可能在多年後才以接合螺栓鬆動或裂縫的形式出現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without long-term monitoring, slab tilt and façade-joint distortion from residual differential shortening are mistaken for workmanship defects and repaired again and again; outrigger forces beyond expectation may surface only years later as loosened connection bolts or cracks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每年以精密水準量測巨柱與核心在代表樓層的高程差，並讀取應變計與接頭位移計，與時間相依分析的預測曲線比較；發展速率異常（例如某支巨柱持續快於其他柱）時，檢查是否有局部超載或材料問題。","textEn":"Each year measure level differences between mega-columns and core on representative floors by precise levelling and read strain gauges and joint displacement gauges, comparing with the predicted time-dependent curves; if a rate is abnormal, such as one column persistently outpacing the others, check for local overloading or material problems.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件包含鎖定時的實測差異、預測的長期曲線、監測點位置與允收範圍，以及超出範圍時的處理流程；監測至少持續到徐變發展趨緩，並由結構顧問定期審閱。","textEn":"Handover documents include the measured difference at lock-off, the predicted long-term curves, monitoring locations and acceptance ranges, and the procedure when values fall outside them; continue monitoring at least until creep growth levels off, with periodic review by the structural consultant.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems\"?","options":["每年以精密水準量測巨柱與核心在代表樓層的高程差，並讀取應變計與接頭位移計，與時間相依分析的預測曲線比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","外伸臂在模型裡有效，實際上就一定照模型分擔。"],"optionsEn":["Each year measure level differences between mega-columns and core on representative floors by precise levelling and read strain gauges and joint displacement gauges, comparing with the predicted time-dependent curves.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","If outriggers work in the model, they must share load exactly as modelled."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每年以精密水準量測巨柱與核心在代表樓層的高程差，並讀取應變計與接頭位移計，與時間相依分析的預測曲線比較；發展速率異常（例如某支巨柱持續快於其他柱）時，檢查是否有局部超載或材料問題。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Each year measure level differences between mega-columns and core on representative floors by precise levelling and read strain gauges and joint displacement gauges, comparing with the predicted time-dependent curves; if a rate is abnormal, such as one column persistently outpacing the others, check for local overloading or material problems. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b063-v13-40","title":"外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"prerequisiteIds":["b063-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長期徐變監測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-term creep monitoring” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沒有長期監測，殘留差異縮短造成的樓板傾斜與帷幕接縫變形會被誤認為施工瑕疵而反覆修補；外伸臂附加力超出預期，也可能在多年後才以接合螺栓鬆動或裂縫的形式出現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without long-term monitoring, slab tilt and façade-joint distortion from residual differential shortening are mistaken for workmanship defects and repaired again and again; outrigger forces beyond expectation may surface only years later as loosened connection bolts or cracks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：長期監測以應變計、精密水準與接頭位移計追蹤這個過程，並與時間相依分析比較；交接文件要讓營運單位知道哪些數值屬於正常發展、何時需要請結構顧問評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Long-term monitoring with strain gauges, precise levelling and joint displacement gauges tracks this process against time-dependent analysis, and handover documents must tell the operator which values are normal development and when to call in the structural consultant.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂鎖定之後，差異縮短的問題就結束了。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once the outriggers are locked, differential shortening is no longer an issue.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b063-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沒有長期監測，殘留差異縮短造成的樓板傾斜與帷幕接縫變形會被誤認為施工瑕疵而反覆修補；外伸臂附加力超出預期，也可能在多年後才以接合螺栓鬆動或裂縫的形式出現。","textEn":"Without long-term monitoring, slab tilt and façade-joint distortion from residual differential shortening are mistaken for workmanship defects and repaired again and again; outrigger forces beyond expectation may surface only years later as loosened connection bolts or cracks.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]},{"id":"b063-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸臂系統的長期縮短監測與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-term shortening monitoring and handover of outrigger systems\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若沒有長期監測，殘留差異縮短造成的樓板傾斜與帷幕接縫變形會被誤認為施工瑕疵而反覆修補；外伸臂附加力超出預期，也可能在多年後才以接合螺栓鬆動或裂縫的形式出現。","外伸臂是把核心「撐住」的水平支撐，與柱子的軸向勁度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Without long-term monitoring, slab tilt and façade-joint distortion from residual differential shortening are mistaken for workmanship defects and repaired again and again.","An outrigger is a horizontal prop that braces the core, regardless of column axial stiffness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若沒有長期監測，殘留差異縮短造成的樓板傾斜與帷幕接縫變形會被誤認為施工瑕疵而反覆修補；外伸臂附加力超出預期，也可能在多年後才以接合螺栓鬆動或裂縫的形式出現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without long-term monitoring, slab tilt and façade-joint distortion from residual differential shortening are mistaken for workmanship defects and repaired again and again; outrigger forces beyond expectation may surface only years later as loosened connection bolts or cracks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-aisc-taipei-101-2002","v13s-aisc-shanghai-tower-2013","v13s-ctbuh-paper-burj-dubai","v13s-ctbuh-shanghai-tower","v13s-constructsteel-shanghai-tower"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
